''   Started.... 11 Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 13 Sep 2026 -- task 3521 phase A: unattended automatic holds (no PLOT panel, no
''               operator advance, no dwell floor), same-lifetime zero per hold (PL-32), overflow-
''               proof accumulators (PL-20), quiescent hold from a started driver (PL-21), booleans
''               as TRUE/FALSE (PL-23), motor frame named on every hold (PL-19), no method-calling
''               ternaries (PL-29)
''   Updated.... 13 Sep 2026 -- task 3521 phase B (SRC_REV 3, fmt 3): a watchdog cog names where
''               a cog-0 stall happened, stops both wheels and ends the session on its own
''   Updated.... 13 Sep 2026 -- task 3521 phase C (SRC_REV 4, fmt 4): SIGNOFF-DECL / SIGNOFF
''               verdicts for R5-CHAR-SENSE, R4-CHAR-RPM, R2-CHAR-ISCALE and R3-CHAR-INTEG
''   Updated.... 13 Sep 2026 -- task 3521 phase D (SRC_REV 5, fmt 5): steering-object phase
''               (R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL / STEERSTART / STEERLIVE) and brake-mode start phase
''               (R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART) after the nine holds
''   Updated.... 14 Sep 2026 -- task 3539 (SRC_REV 6, fmt 6; PL-44/PL-47): removed every trap used
''               to capture a normal return -- steerStartTrapped/steerStartCall,
''               steerDriveTrapped/steerDriveCall and brakeStartTrapped/brakeStartCall are gone;
''               steering.start()/driveAtPower()/startEx() are called UNTRAPPED and judged by
''               their returned value. main()'s \bRunSession() is the top-level trap, and its
''               value is now printed on every run, not only on abort (BC-END trap field). The
''               one other trap is bClaimsFreeCheck()'s declared abort-path probe: a leaked PL-36
''               claim is a library abort, so it must print FALSE rather than end the run. P5:
''               BC-STEER's "aborted" field is replaced by "drive_done", reporting
''               driveAtPower()'s own value directly instead of folding a wrong value into an
''               abort flag. P6: R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL no longer runs a premature steerStop()
''               before bClaimsFreeCheck() when the STEERFAIL start's real return happens to
''               differ from -1 -- that steerStop() was masking the PL-36 leak check it exists
''               to catch. R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART's cog-id guard (measureBrakeStart()) now compares
''               against a real, untrapped return instead of a stuck trapped 0, so the cell can
''               PASS or FAIL instead of always NOMEAS.
''   Updated.... 16 Sep 2026 -- task 3560 (SRC_REV 7, fmt 7; Visit 4): the front cog (task 3513) owns
''               every driver command and releases a synced standalone driver itself inside
''               startEx(), so this file no longer calls cogatn(): R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART starts the
''               wheel with start(), then holdAtStop(TRUE) at rest, which the driver applies through
''               the same checkstop -> initAngleFmHall path the brake-mode start took. Nothing aborts
''               any more (task 3554), so bClaimsFreeCheck() starts untrapped and its trap and
''               completion flag are deleted. New cell R16-CHAR-STEERERR and record BC-STEERERR: the
''               failed steering start's getError() names the wheel that failed (task 3555).
''   Updated.... 18 Sep 2026 -- task 3517 (SRC_REV 8): style guide 5.4.1 -- every method returning one
''               boolean is named is/has/b (e.g. bRunSession(), isWheelReady()). No record changes.
''   Updated.... 19 Sep 2026 -- task 3574 (SRC_REV 11, fmt 8): records are assembled by isp_bench_log
''               (benchLog on cog 0, wdLog on the watchdog cog) instead of this file's two private copies
''               (PL-53) -- the same algorithm, so every record is byte-identical. BC-SENSE drops min_mV,
''               max_mV and watts_mW, which fed nothing. A hold that reached steadiness by TIMEOUT now
''               makes its SENSE, RPM and ISCALE instances NOMEAS instead of judging a window that may
''               hold the end of the ramp (MEASURED: 0 of 24 motion holds have ever timed out).
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ WHY THIS RUN

  Bench Pass 1 (DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-09-12/CHAR-RUN-EVALUATION.md) ran this binary as an
  operator-held, meter-read session. The current channel is now confirmed (sense_i_mV is true
  millivolts, about 150 mV/A on Rev B), so every hold is now measured from the driver's own
  telemetry, unattended, with no meter and no keypress.

  FRAME. Every hold is in MOTOR frame: the signed motor increment is what is commanded, and
  forwardIsReverse() is never called on either wheel. Every BC-HOLD record carries the signed
  increment, a robot_dir field (LEFT + = robot forward, RIGHT + = robot reverse, because the two
  motors are mounted mirror-image), and frame,MOTOR. Every caption names its frame (PL-19).

  THE IDLE WHEEL IS NEVER RUNNING. Each hold stop()s both wheels and then start()s only the wheel
  under test, so the other wheel has no driver cog, its pins are released and its bridges float.
  holdAtStop() appears nowhere; init()'s default SM_FLOAT gives a floating stop.

  EACH HOLD IS ITS OWN DRIVER LIFETIME. The driver calibrates its ADCs at start (PL-32), so a sense
  zero is valid only within the lifetime it was read in. Every hold, including the quiescent hold
  0, starts its wheel, then reads its own zero at zero command, then measures -- never a zero from
  before a restart.

  HOLD SEQUENCE (per motion hold):
   (1) stop both wheels, start the hold's wheel, wait ready (READY_TIMEOUT_MS), startSenseCog()
       (task 3513: it returns the front cog start() already launched, and starts nothing)
   (2) zero: ZERO_SAMPLES x SAMPLE_MS at zero command, same lifetime
   (3) command the signed increment, wait DCS_AT_SPEED (ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS), waitForSteady()
       (hall-rate confirmation, STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS), settle SETTLE_MS
   (4) sample every SAMPLE_MS for WINDOW_MS; testGetRpm() read at the window's end, which is at
       least SETTLE_MS + WINDOW_MS = 4 s after AT_SPEED (rpm needs ~1 s of motion to fill)
   (5) command zero, wait STOPPED (STOP_TIMEOUT_MS), stop the wheel, and ONLY THEN print
  Hold 0 is steps (1), (2), (4) and (5) on HOLD_ZERO_SIDE, started and held at zero command.
  A bounded wait that times out becomes that hold's result token; it never aborts the run.

  NO timed window (zero, AT_SPEED wait, steady wait, settle, sample window, stop wait) contains a
  debug() statement or a call to a library method that emits one. Every record is emitted after
  the wheel has stopped.

  NO STOP TIMER. Motion is commanded with testDriveAtMotorIncrement() alone; stopAfterTime() is
  never called, so the front cog never zeroes a command behind this file's back.

  PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY. emergencyCutoff() latches until
  clearEmergency() since task 3556 (finding S-4 retired), but it is a software stop, not a panic
  button; this file does not call it.

  WATCHDOG (task 3521 phase B). Unattended bench binaries carry a watchdog: scan run 5's cog 0
  stopped emitting debug mid-run while the P2 kept running. A second cog watches cog 0's
  heartbeat (beat(), on every loop pass and around every library call and record). If it does
  not advance for WD_STALL_MS, the watchdog snapshots where cog 0 was and both wheels' state,
  stops both wheels, emits BC-WATCHDOG, BC-WATCHDOG2 and BC-END exit WATCHDOG, prints the end
  marker and idles. It touches no motor before it declares a stall. BC-WDSTART, the first record,
  says whether it started; if it did not, the run proceeds unwatched and says so.

  HOW IT IS RUN

      tools/bench-run.sh char

  -D BENCH_CFG selects isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench.spin2 for the banner's cfg_id only -- the
  pin bases, voltage and detection mode this file drives are compile-time constants (CON
  { bench target }) so it compiles under every block of isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2.

  RECORD DISCIPLINE

  Tag-first, comma-separated name,value pairs, all tags prefixed BC-. Every record type always
  emits every field in the same order; absence is the token NA, never a missing field and never
  a 0. Booleans are the tokens TRUE/FALSE (PL-23). Every numeric field is clamped to a stated
  width and every token to a stated length, so each record's worst case is a stated number of
  bytes under 280 (the longest record measured intact through one debug(zstr_())). The worst
  case of each record is stated at its emitter.

  SIGN-OFF VERDICTS (task 3521 phase C; DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md sec B). Right after
  BC-PLAN, one SIGNOFF-DECL per cell this binary judges. On cog 0's normal end path, after both
  wheels are stopped and before BC-END, one SIGNOFF per instance of every declared cell, computed
  only from the per-hold results. A verdict is PASS only when the instance was measured AND its
  value lies in lo..hi; unmeasured is NOMEAS with n 0 and measured NA, never PASS. On the watchdog
  path no verdict is emitted: the host reads a declared cell with no verdict as NOMEAS.

  STEERING AND BRAKE-START PHASES (task 3521 phase D; design sec A.4 rows 10 and 13). Only when
  preflight passed, after the nine holds:
   (1) runSteeringPhase(): both wheelL/wheelR stopped first, because this file's wheels and the
       steering object's own two share the pin-claim registry (PL-18). R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL starts
       the steering object with exactly one free cog, and R16-CHAR-STEERERR reads which wheel
       getError() names for it; R10-CHAR-STEERSTART starts it normally and
       waits for both wheels' driver state; R10-CHAR-STEERLIVE drives both through the public
       driveAtPower() for PREFLIGHT_MS and judges each wheel's raw hall-tick delta. BC-STEER and
       BC-STEERERR are printed after the stop wait and steering.stop().
   (2) runBrakeStartPhase(): steering stopped first, then per motor x sign on this file's own
       wheels (motor frame): start() -> ready -> holdAtStop(TRUE) at rest -> BRAKE_SETTLE_MS ->
       signed PREFLIGHT_INCRE for PREFLIGHT_MS -> zero -> stopped -> holdAtStop(FALSE) -> stop().
       One BC-BRAKE per instance, printed after that instance's wheel is stopped.
  The timed PREFLIGHT_MS windows contain no debug() from this file; the library calls that start
  them (driveAtPower(), testDriveAtMotorIncrement()) print their own lines just before the wait,
  exactly as the preflight nudge already does, and the steering object's front cog prints state
  changes from its own cog. Neither window times anything but a tick delta.
}

CON { build identity }

    SRC_REV     = 11                                       ' hand-bumped whenever this file changes
    FMT_VERSION = 8                                         ' BC- record-format version (3: phase B adds BC-WDSTART, BC-WATCHDOG, BC-WATCHDOG2, BC-END exit WATCHDOG; 4: phase C adds SIGNOFF-DECL and SIGNOFF sf 1; 5: phase D adds BC-STEER, BC-BRAKE and four sign-off cells; 6: task 3539 -- removed BC-STEER's "aborted" field (replaced by "drive_done") and BC-BRAKE's "abort" field: every trap used to capture a normal return is gone, so there is nothing left to name as aborted; 7: task 3560 -- adds BC-STEERERR and cell R16-CHAR-STEERERR, no existing record changes shape; 8: task 3574 -- BC-SENSE drops min_mV, max_mV and watts_mW)

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                  ' every top in this tree runs at 270 MHz
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ
    MS_PER_SEC = 1000

' waitms() must not be asked for more than $8000_0000 clocks (p2kbSpin2Waitms, as cited by
' test_bench_scan.spin2 -- not re-read in this session, no p2kb available: UNVERIFIED here), so
' milliseconds <= $8000_0000 / (CLK_FREQ / MS_PER_SEC) = 7_953 ms at 270 MHz. +/ is the UNSIGNED
' divide: $8000_0000 is -2_147_483_648 as a signed long, so / would give -7_953. Every waitms()
' argument in this file is a compile-time constant at or under this ceiling: SAMPLE_MS 5,
' STEADY_SAMPLE_MS 250, PREFLIGHT_MS 700, WD_POLL_MS 250, WD_IDLE_MS 1_000. A wait longer than
' the ceiling must be a repeat of a shorter one (the watchdog's idle-forever loop is).
    WAITMS_MAX_MS = $8000_0000 +/ (CLK_FREQ / MS_PER_SEC)   ' 7_953 ms at 270 MHz

CON { bench target -- the fixed dual 6.5in Rev B 18.5V rig }

' Hardcoded rather than read from `user`: a dual-motor config block defines LEFT_MOTOR_BASE /
' RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE and no ONLY_MOTOR_BASE, and vice versa, so reading either through `user`
' would fail to compile under whichever block is active. The library's own PINS_*/PWR_*/BRD_*
' constants are legal under every config block.
    LEFT_TEST_BASE  = wheelL.PINS_P32_P47                    ' the LEFT board is at P32, measured 2026-09-11
    RIGHT_TEST_BASE = wheelL.PINS_P16_P31
    TEST_VOLTAGE    = wheelL.PWR_18p5V
    TEST_DET_MODE   = wheelL.BRD_AUTO_DET
    MAX_COG_ID      = 7                                      ' start() returns a cog id 0..7, or -1

CON { drive speed -- NO increment may exceed DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE }

' isp_bldc_motor.spin2 confgurePowerLimits(): 147_000_000 is the 18.5V motor-increment ceiling.
    DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE = 147_000_000
    QTR_SPEED_INCRE     = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 4           ' 36_750_000, quarter speed
    HALF_SPEED_INCRE    = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 2           ' 73_500_000, half speed
    PREFLIGHT_INCRE     = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 8           ' 18_375_000, gentle nudge

CON { sampling, windows and wait bounds }

    SAMPLE_MS          = 5                                  ' telemetry poll cadence in every timed loop
    ZERO_SAMPLES       = 200                                ' same-lifetime zero: 200 x 5 ms, ~1 s
    SETTLE_MS          = 1_000                              ' after AT_SPEED (and the rate check), before the window
    ' WINDOW_MS: 3 s at ~99 ticks/s (quarter speed) is ~297 hall ticks, just over 3 wheel
    ' revolutions (90 ticks/rev) -- the same span the offset scan uses for a fine point
    ' (WIN_TICKS_FINE = 270) -- so the mean averages whole revolutions of hall/cogging ripple
    ' rather than a fraction of one; ~600 samples at SAMPLE_MS. It also exceeds the ~1 s rpm
    ' averaging window, so testGetRpm() at its end reads a full window of steady motion.
    WINDOW_MS          = 3_000
    READY_TIMEOUT_MS   = 2_000                              ' driver cog reports ready after start()
    ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS = 4_000                              ' AT_SPEED observed ~0.9 s (1/4) / ~1.3 s (1/2) in the scan
    STOP_TIMEOUT_MS    = 3_000                              ' ramp-down ~0.37 s (1/4) / ~0.75 s (1/2)
    STEADY_SAMPLE_MS   = 250                                ' waitForSteady() hall-rate sample period
    STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES = 4
    STEADY_TOL_PCT     = 5
    STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS  = 6_000                              ' waitForSteady() bound
    PREFLIGHT_MS       = 700                                ' preflight nudge duration per wheel
    RATE_X10_SCALE     = 10_000                             ' ticks * this / ms = ticks per second x10
    RATE_TICKS_CAP     = 99_999                             ' ticks clamp before * RATE_X10_SCALE: 999_990_000 < 2^31
    X10                = 10

CON { overflow-proof running mean (PL-20) }

' Every accumulator is an EXACT incremental mean held as (mean, remainder, count), with the
' invariant  sum == mean * count + remainder,  0 <= remainder < count  -- the true sum is never
' stored, so it cannot overflow however long the window runs or however large the scale.
' Adding sample x (clamped to +/-ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT) at new count n computes
'     delta = remainder + x - mean
' and then mean += floor(delta / n), remainder = delta - floor(delta / n) * n.
' Bound: remainder < n <= ACC_COUNT_CAP, |x| <= ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT, and |mean| <= ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT
' (a floor mean of clamped samples), so
'     |delta| < ACC_COUNT_CAP + 2 * ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT = 100_000_000 + 1_000_000_000
'             = 1_100_000_000  <  2_147_483_647 (POSX).
' ACC_COUNT_CAP at SAMPLE_MS = 5 ms is 500_000 s (~5.8 days) of samples; past it further samples
' are not added (the count stops, so the record still states how many samples the mean holds).
' ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT is ~100x the pre-S-3 scale's largest reading (~5.2e6 mV), so no real sample
' is ever clamped. The x10 mean is (mean clamped to +/-ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT) * 10 + remainder * 10
' / count, where remainder * 10 < ACC_COUNT_CAP * 10 = 1e9 < POSX.
    ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT   = 500_000_000
    ACC_COUNT_CAP      = 100_000_000
    ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT = 99_999_999

  ' Accumulator slots:
  '  ACC_ZERO  - sense_i_mV at zero command, same driver lifetime
  '  ACC_SENSE - sense_i_mV over the sample window
  '  ACC_AMPS  - getCurrent() amps x 10_000 over the window
  '  ACC_DUTY  - duty over the window
  '  ACC_ERR   - position error over the window
    #0, ACC_ZERO, ACC_SENSE, ACC_AMPS, ACC_DUTY, ACC_ERR
    ACC_SLOTS = ACC_ERR + 1

CON ' ---- Hold Sequence ----
  ' The nine-hold run: quiescent zero, then left/right x +/- increment at quarter speed, then
  ' left/right x +/- again at half speed. HOLD_LAST selects how far the run goes.
    #0, HOLD_ZERO, HOLD_L_FWD_QTR, HOLD_L_REV_QTR, HOLD_R_FWD_QTR, HOLD_R_REV_QTR, ...
        HOLD_L_FWD_HALF, HOLD_L_REV_HALF, HOLD_R_FWD_HALF, HOLD_R_REV_HALF
    HOLD_COUNT = HOLD_R_REV_HALF + 1
    HOLD_LAST  = HOLD_R_REV_HALF                            ' edit to stop the run earlier
    HOLD_ZERO_SIDE = SIDE_LEFT                              ' hold 0's driver: LEFT, started at zero command (PL-21)

CON ' ---- Motor-Side / Result Enums ----
  ' Which wheel a hold drives:
  '  SIDE_NONE  - no wheel
  '  SIDE_LEFT  - wheelL started, wheelR not running
  '  SIDE_RIGHT - wheelR started, wheelL not running
    #0, SIDE_NONE, SIDE_LEFT, SIDE_RIGHT

  ' Hold result (the first cause is kept, except that a fault or a lost cog always overwrites):
  '  RES_OK             - every step completed
  '  RES_NOT_RUN        - the hold was never reached
  '  RES_NO_COG         - start() failed, or the driver cog was not running when read
  '  RES_READY_TIMEOUT  - the driver did not report ready within READY_TIMEOUT_MS
  '  RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT - DCS_AT_SPEED not reached within ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS
  '  RES_FAULT          - the driver faulted
  '  RES_STOP_TIMEOUT   - STOPPED not reached within STOP_TIMEOUT_MS after the zero command
    #0, RES_OK, RES_NOT_RUN, RES_NO_COG, RES_READY_TIMEOUT, RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT, ...
        RES_FAULT, RES_STOP_TIMEOUT

CON { record widths -- every numeric field is clamped to one of these }

    LIM_TINY  = benchLog.LIM_TINY  ' prints at most 4 bytes: -999
    LIM_SMALL = benchLog.LIM_SMALL  ' prints at most 7 bytes: -99_999
    LIM_MID   = benchLog.LIM_MID  ' prints at most 10 bytes: -9_999_999
    LIM_BIG   = benchLog.LIM_BIG  ' prints at most 12 bytes: -999_999_999

    ' token field length limits (a longer token prints as "?")
    TOKMAX_MOTOR   = 5
    TOKMAX_ROBOT   = 4
    TOKMAX_FRAME   = 5
    TOKMAX_RUNG    = 4
    TOKMAX_RESULT  = 14
    TOKMAX_STEADY  = 7
    TOKMAX_CFG     = 5
    TOKMAX_BOARD   = 7
    TOKMAX_EXIT    = 8
    TOKMAX_CAPTION = 96

CON ' ---- Sign-off Verdicts ----
  ' Task 3521 phase C. Record contract: DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md sec B.1, sign-off format 1.
  ' Every limit is compiled in and printed in each record, so the host catches a stale build.
    SF_VERSION = 1

  ' The todo-mcp task that owns each cell (manifest sec A.4) prints as a plain text token -- the
  ' sSfTask* DAT strings -- never through benchLog.numField(), whose digit grouping would print 3_503
  ' where Tier 0 prints 3503 for the same field.
    TOKMAX_TASK = 5

  ' Token field length limits (design sec B.3); a longer token prints "?" and cannot match a cell
    TOKMAX_BIN       = 6
    TOKMAX_CELL      = 20
    TOKMAX_CRIT      = 18
    TOKMAX_UNITS     = 8
    TOKMAX_SFVERDICT = 9

  ' R5-CHAR-SENSE, crit NET_VS_PASS1_PCT, units PCT_X10.
  ' DERIVED (design sec A.5-d): 1.5 x the largest run-to-run deviation MEASURED at a matching hold
  ' on default offsets in scan run 5 (L -1/2: +10.2 %) = 15.3 %, taken as +/-15.0 %.
    SENSE_PCT_X10_LO = -150
    SENSE_PCT_X10_HI = 150
  ' MEASURED: least-squares fit sense_mV = 150.1 x meter_A + 9.1 over Pass 1's eight motion holds
  ' (DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-09-12/CHAR-RUN-EVALUATION.md sec 2), held as mV x10 per amp. The
  ' expected net omits the 9.1 intercept: net is already minus a same-lifetime zero (sec A.5-d).
    PASS1_FIT_MV_X10_PER_A = 1501
    MA_PER_A               = 1000
    PCT_X10_PER_UNIT       = 1000                           ' (net - expected) x this / expected = percent x10
  ' |net - expected| is clamped to this before x PCT_X10_PER_UNIT: 2_000_000 x 1000 = 2e9 < POSX.
  ' A real post-S-3 net is under 10_000 (1 V); the clamp is reached only by a scale regression,
  ' and it keeps the sign, so such a value still lands far outside the band.
    SENSE_DIFF_X10_LIMIT   = 2_000_000

  ' R4-CHAR-RPM, crit RPM_ERR, units RPM.
  ' DERIVED (design sec A.5-c): the library's integer rpm truncates (<= 1 rpm), and its ~1 s window
  ' differs from this file's window by ~1 tick/s = 60 / 90 = 0.67 rpm; 1.67 rounded up to 2.
    RPM_ERR_LO = -2
    RPM_ERR_HI = 2
  ' expected rpm = ticks_per_s x 60 / 90 = (rate_x10 / 10) x 60 / 90 = rate_x10 / 15, where 90 is
  ' the 6.5in motor's hall ticks per revolution (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 getRotationCount(): "ticks /
  ' 90 (6.5in wheel)"). + RPM_ROUND_HALF_X10 makes the division round-to-nearest: 15 is odd, so no
  ' non-negative integer rate sits exactly on a half.
    HALL_TICKS_PER_REV = 90
    SECS_PER_MIN       = 60
    RATE_X10_PER_RPM   = (X10 * HALL_TICKS_PER_REV) / SECS_PER_MIN     ' 15
    RPM_ROUND_HALF_X10 = RATE_X10_PER_RPM / 2                          ' 7

  ' R2-CHAR-ISCALE, crit RSENSE_IMPLIED, units COUNT (mV per amp).
  ' DERIVED (design sec A.4 row 2): getCurrent() = sense_i_mV x 10_000 / rSenseForBoard
  ' (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 getCurrent()), rSenseForBoard 150 on Rev B and 5 on Rev A (its comment,
  ' and init()'s REV_A/REV_B selection); +/-10 % of 150 absorbs per-sample truncation and the
  ' non-atomic sampling of two window means, and a Rev A misdetect's 5 cannot pass.
    RSENSE_IMPLIED_LO = 135
    RSENSE_IMPLIED_HI = 165
  ' raw_mV_x10 x 1000 / amps_x10k = (10 mV)(1000) / (10_000 A) = mV / A
    ISCALE_RATIO_SCALE = 1000
  ' |raw_mV_x10| at or under this: x ISCALE_RATIO_SCALE = 2e9 < POSX. The ADC spans 3.3 V (raw
  ' under 33_000); larger is reachable only by a scale regression, handled without overflow.
    ISCALE_DIRECT_RAW_X10_MAX = 2_000_000
    ISCALE_QUOT_MAX           = LIM_BIG / ISCALE_RATIO_SCALE              ' 999_999: x 1000 fits LIM_BIG

  ' R3-CHAR-INTEG, crit MISSED_ILLEGAL_SUM, units COUNT.
  ' MEASURED (design sec A.4 row 3): missed 0 and illegal 0 at every start and every point of scan
  ' run 5. DERIVED: at <= 212 ticks/s against the driver's 43.9 kHz loop no transition is skipped.
    INTEG_SUM_LO = 0
    INTEG_SUM_HI = 0

CON ' ---- Steering and Brake-Start Phases ----
  ' Task 3521 phase D. Design DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md sec A.4 rows 10 and 13, sec H.2.

  ' Liveness floor for R10-CHAR-STEERLIVE and R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART, TICKS.
  ' MEASURED: a PREFLIGHT_INCRE (18_375_000) nudge held PREFLIGHT_MS moved 13 ticks
  ' (DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-09-13/debug_260913-120844.log:46). DERIVED (design sec A.5-f): half of
  ' it, 6. PL-22's parked cogs move exactly 0, so the floor rejects them and tolerates ramp spread.
    LIVENESS_MIN_TICKS = 6

  ' R10-CHAR-STEERLIVE drive power. DERIVED from isp_steering_2wheel.spin2 driveAtPower() ->
  ' isp_bldc_motor.spin2 driveAtPowerEx(): power is clamped to [-100, 100], then to
  ' [-maxSpeed, maxSpeed] (init() sets maxSpeed 75; nothing here calls setMaxSpeed(), so 13 passes
  ' unclamped), negated for the right wheel (forwardIsReverse()), then incrementForPower() ->
  ' map(power, 1, 100, minFwdIncreAtPwr, maxFwdIncreAtPwr). confgurePowerLimits() gives the 6.5in
  ' motor at PWR_18p5V min 544_628 and max 147_000_000 (DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE). map()'s integer slope
  ' is (147_000_000 - 544_628) / (100 - 1) = 146_455_372 / 99 = 1_479_347 (truncated), and the
  ' result is 544_628 + 1_479_347 x (power - 1):
  '   power 12 -> 16_817_445 (1_557_555 under PREFLIGHT_INCRE)
  '   power 13 -> 18_296_792 (   78_208 under PREFLIGHT_INCRE)  <- nearest
  '   power 14 -> 19_776_139 (1_401_139 over  PREFLIGHT_INCRE)
  ' The negative branch maps to -18_296_792 by the same arithmetic, so the right wheel's commanded
  ' increment is the same magnitude. STEER_CMD_INCRE repeats map()'s arithmetic at compile time.
    STEER_POWER         = 13
    POWER_FULL          = 100                               ' driveAtPowerEx() power ceiling
    POWER_MIN_STEP      = 1                                 ' map()'s inMin for a forward request
    LIB_MIN_FWD_INCRE   = 544_628                           ' confgurePowerLimits(): 6.5in minFwdIncreAtPwr
    STEER_CMD_INCRE     = LIB_MIN_FWD_INCRE + ((DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE - LIB_MIN_FWD_INCRE) / (POWER_FULL - POWER_MIN_STEP)) * (STEER_POWER - POWER_MIN_STEP)

  ' R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL, crit RET_NEG_NOLEAK, units BOOL. TRUE when start() returned STEERFAIL_RET
  ' (DERIVED from isp_steering_2wheel.spin2 start(): a failed motor start stops whichever motor did
  ' start and returns -1, :124-133) AND the free-cog count is back to baseline AND this file's own
  ' wheels can claim both bench bases afterwards (PL-36: a failed start must release its pin claim)
  ' AND nothing aborted.
    STEERFAIL_RET          = -1
    STEERFAIL_MIN_BASELINE = 1                              ' fewer free cogs than this: NOMEAS

  ' R10-CHAR-STEERSTART, crit STEER_START_COG, units BOOL. TRUE when start() returned a cog id in
  ' STEERSTART_COG_LO..STEERSTART_COG_HI (DERIVED: the sense cog's id on success,
  ' isp_steering_2wheel.spin2:170) AND both wheels left DCS_Unknown AND nothing aborted.
    STEERSTART_COG_LO = 0
    STEERSTART_COG_HI = MAX_COG_ID

  ' Every phase D sign-off instance stands on one start, one drive window or one brake start.
    SIGNOFF_ONE_INSTANCE = 1

  ' Free-cog counting (design sec A.5-a): cogspin() spacers until one returns < 0 (not == -1: the
  ' library documents a $8000_xxxx exhaustion form, isp_bldc_motor.spin2:110), then cogstop() them.
  ' spacerIdle() has no params, returns or locals and calls only waitms(); 32 longs covers its frame
  ' plus the interpreter's per-call bookkeeping, which is not visible in this repo (UNVERIFIED).
    SPACER_MAX         = MAX_COG_ID + 1
    SPACER_STACK_LONGS = 32

  ' R16-CHAR-STEERERR, crit WHEEL_NAMED, units BOOL (task 3555). With one free cog the left driver
  ' (started first) takes it and the right driver's coginit() fails, recording ERR_NO_FREE_COG in the
  ' right wheel's slot for this cog; getError()'s three results must name the right wheel and not the
  ' left. DERIVED from isp_steering_2wheel.spin2 start() and isp_bldc_motor.spin2 launchDriver().
    STEERERR_FAILED_WHEEL_CODE = wheelL.ERR_NO_FREE_COG
    STEERERR_OK_CODE           = wheelL.NO_ERROR

  ' R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART: holdAtStop(TRUE) is applied by the driver at rest on its next drive pass
  ' (the stopped path compares stop_mode with curr_stop every pass and calls checkstop on a change);
  ' 50 ms is about 95 drive passes (522.7 us each, PL-50) before the brake is judged.
    BRAKE_SETTLE_MS    = 50

  ' Brake-start instances, motor frame (no forwardIsReverse()):
  '  BRK_L_POS - LEFT motor, + PREFLIGHT_INCRE
  '  BRK_L_NEG - LEFT motor, - PREFLIGHT_INCRE
  '  BRK_R_POS - RIGHT motor, + PREFLIGHT_INCRE
  '  BRK_R_NEG - RIGHT motor, - PREFLIGHT_INCRE
    #0, BRK_L_POS, BRK_L_NEG, BRK_R_POS, BRK_R_NEG
    BRAKE_COUNT = BRK_R_NEG + 1

CON ' ---- Cog-0 Progress Checkpoints ----
  ' The watchdog heartbeat contract, task 3521 phase B. beat(CP_*) records the smallest statement
  ' group cog 0 is inside, so a stall's last checkpoint (BC-WATCHDOG) pins it there. A CP_LIB_* id
  ' is set immediately before AND immediately after its library call, so a stall parked on it is
  ' inside that call or in the few statements of its wrapper's return path:
  '  CP_MAIN_INIT       - main(): watchdog start, BC-WDSTART, initRun()
  '  CP_MAIN_BANNER     - main(): emitBanner()
  '  CP_MAIN_PLAN       - main(): emitPlan() and emitSignoffDecls()
  '  CP_MAIN_RUN        - main(): entering bRunSession()
  '  CP_MAIN_SHUTDOWN   - main(): bRunSession() returned or aborted; watchdog stop, both stop()s
  '  CP_MAIN_END        - main(): SIGNOFF verdicts, BC-END and the end marker
  '  CP_PREFLIGHT_LEFT  - bPreflightWheels(), LEFT wheel pass, including its PREFLIGHT_MS nudge
  '  CP_PREFLIGHT_RIGHT - bPreflightWheels(), RIGHT wheel pass, including its PREFLIGHT_MS nudge
  '  CP_HOLD            - runAllHolds()/measureHold(): one hold's sequencing between its steps
  '  CP_START_SIDE      - startSide(): stop both, then start the named wheel
  '  CP_LIB_START       - brackets start()
  '  CP_LOOP_WAITREADY  - one pass of bWaitUntilReady()
  '  CP_LIB_STARTSENSE  - brackets startSenseCog()
  '  CP_LOOP_ZERO       - one pass of measureZero()
  '  CP_LIB_COMMAND     - brackets testDriveAtMotorIncrement()
  '  CP_LOOP_ATSPEED    - one pass of bWaitAtSpeed()
  '  CP_LOOP_STEADY     - one pass of waitForSteady()
  '  CP_LOOP_SETTLE     - one pass of bSettleHold()
  '  CP_LOOP_WINDOW     - one pass of sampleWindow()
  '  CP_LOOP_WAITSTOP   - one pass of bWaitStoppedFor()
  '  CP_LIB_STOP_LEFT   - brackets wheelL.stop()
  '  CP_LIB_STOP_RIGHT  - brackets wheelR.stop()
  '  CP_LIB_INTEGRITY   - brackets getHallIntegrityCounts()
  '  CP_LIB_DRVSTATE    - brackets getDriverState()
  '  CP_LIB_COGUP       - brackets testGetMotorCog()
  '  CP_LIB_ISREADY     - brackets isReady()
  '  CP_LIB_ISSTOPPED   - brackets isStopped()
  '  CP_LIB_TELEMETRY   - brackets testGetTelemetry()
  '  CP_LIB_CURRENT     - brackets getCurrent()
  '  CP_LIB_TICKS       - brackets getRawHallTicks()
  '  CP_LIB_OFFSETS     - brackets testGetFwdRevIndep()
  '  CP_LIB_RPM         - brackets testGetRpm()
  '  CP_LIB_BOARDTYPE   - brackets getBoardType()
  '  CP_LIB_CONSTANTS   - brackets testGetDriveConstants()
  '  CP_EMIT            - brackets lineEmit(), so every BC- record from cog 0
  '  CP_NOTE            - brackets a plain debug() note line that is not a BC- record
  ' Task 3521 phase D, appended so no earlier id renumbers:
  '  CP_STEER           - runSteeringPhase(): sequencing between its steps
  '  CP_SPACER_LOOP     - one pass of occupySpacers() or releaseSpacers()
  '  CP_LIB_STEER_START - brackets steering.start()
  '  CP_LOOP_STEER_RDY  - one pass of bWaitSteerReady()
  '  CP_STEER_DRIVE     - brackets steering.driveAtPower(), and the PREFLIGHT_MS steering window
  '  CP_LIB_STEER_STOP  - brackets steering.stopMotors() and steering.stop()
  '  CP_LOOP_STEER_STOP - one pass of bWaitSteerStopped()
  '  CP_LIB_STEER_READ  - brackets steering.testGetDriverState(), testGetRawHallTicks(), isStopped()
  '  CP_BRAKE           - runBrakeStartPhase()/measureBrakeStart(): sequencing between steps
  '  CP_LIB_BRAKE_START - brackets the brake phase's wheel start()
  '  CP_LIB_HOLDATSTOP  - brackets wheel holdAtStop()
  '  CP_BRAKE_SETTLE    - brackets the BRAKE_SETTLE_MS wait after holdAtStop(TRUE) (task 3560; this id was CP_COGATN)
  '  CP_BRAKE_DRIVE     - brackets the PREFLIGHT_MS brake-start window
  '  CP_LIB_STEER_ERROR - brackets steering.getError() (task 3560, appended)
    #0, CP_MAIN_INIT, CP_MAIN_BANNER, CP_MAIN_PLAN, CP_MAIN_RUN, CP_MAIN_SHUTDOWN, CP_MAIN_END, ...
        CP_PREFLIGHT_LEFT, CP_PREFLIGHT_RIGHT, CP_HOLD, CP_START_SIDE, CP_LIB_START, ...
        CP_LOOP_WAITREADY, CP_LIB_STARTSENSE, CP_LOOP_ZERO, CP_LIB_COMMAND, CP_LOOP_ATSPEED, ...
        CP_LOOP_STEADY, CP_LOOP_SETTLE, CP_LOOP_WINDOW, CP_LOOP_WAITSTOP, CP_LIB_STOP_LEFT, ...
        CP_LIB_STOP_RIGHT, CP_LIB_INTEGRITY, CP_LIB_DRVSTATE, CP_LIB_COGUP, CP_LIB_ISREADY, ...
        CP_LIB_ISSTOPPED, CP_LIB_TELEMETRY, CP_LIB_CURRENT, CP_LIB_TICKS, CP_LIB_OFFSETS, ...
        CP_LIB_RPM, CP_LIB_BOARDTYPE, CP_LIB_CONSTANTS, CP_EMIT, CP_NOTE, ...
        CP_STEER, CP_SPACER_LOOP, CP_LIB_STEER_START, CP_LOOP_STEER_RDY, CP_STEER_DRIVE, ...
        CP_LIB_STEER_STOP, CP_LOOP_STEER_STOP, CP_LIB_STEER_READ, CP_BRAKE, CP_LIB_BRAKE_START, ...
        CP_LIB_HOLDATSTOP, CP_BRAKE_SETTLE, CP_BRAKE_DRIVE, CP_LIB_STEER_ERROR

    TOKMAX_CP = 10                                          ' longest checkpoint token, e.g. STOP_RIGHT

CON ' ---- Watchdog Cog ----
  ' WD_STALL_MS must exceed the longest legitimate gap cog 0 can leave between two beats, on every
  ' path. Desk trace, task 3521 phase B -- every wait and every library call cog 0 makes, with its
  ' worst case read from source (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 unless named):
  '   waitms(SAMPLE_MS = 5)          one per pass of bWaitUntilReady, measureZero, bWaitAtSpeed,
  '                                  bSettleHold, sampleWindow, bWaitStoppedFor; beat on every pass
  '   waitms(STEADY_SAMPLE_MS = 250) one per pass of waitForSteady; beat on every pass
  '   waitms(PREFLIGHT_MS = 700)     the preflight nudge, beat before and after: THE LONGEST GAP
  '   start()           startEx(): stop() when this instance holds a claim, init(), coginit().
  '                     init() calls getBoardType() on a not-running instance: waitms(1) plus
  '                     DETECT_READ_COUNT = 500 pinread()s (its own measured Rev B figure, ~100
  '                     reads in ~70 us, puts all 500 under 1 ms), float arithmetic including
  '                     isp_dist_utils (no waits), and about 12 debug() lines (~1.2 KB). Under
  '                     150 ms even at 115_200 baud. Task 3513 adds the front cog's cogspin() and
  '                     its first-pass handshake (FRONT_START_TIMEOUT_MS 100), and task 3556 the
  '                     rest-zero capture (REST_ZERO_SAMPLE_COUNT 200 x 5 ms = 1_000 ms): <= 1_250 ms
  '   stop()            EXIT posted to the front cog (REQ_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS 20), cogstop()s and
  '                     pinclear()s; no debug() unless the front cog failed to answer
  '   startSenseCog()   a hub read: it returns the front cog start() launched (task 3513)
  '   getBoardType()    with this wheel's driver running (startHoldWheel only calls it then):
  '                     returns the start-time revision plus one debug() line; no wait
  '   testDriveAtMotorIncrement() -> setTargetAccel(): one debug() line; no wait
  '   testGetDriveConstants(), testGetMotorCog(), isReady(), isStopped(), getDriverState(),
  '   testGetTelemetry(), getCurrent(), getRawHallTicks(), getHallIntegrityCounts(),
  '   testGetFwdRevIndep(), testGetRpm() -- hub reads (getCurrent() adds a float multiply); no wait
  '   lineEmit()        one debug(zstr_()) of at most 280 bytes: under 25 ms even at 115_200 baud
  ' Task 3521 phase D adds (isp_steering_2wheel.spin2 unless named):
  '   steering.start()  success path: two startOwned() (each as start() above without the front cog
  '                     or rest zero, <= 150 ms), waitms(100), cogatn(), one shared rest-zero capture
  '                     (1_000 ms), cogspin() of the front cog and its handshake (<= 100 ms):
  '                     <= 2 x 150 + 100 + 1_000 + 100 = 1_500 ms. Failure path: at most two
  '                     startOwned() and two stop()s: <= 400 ms
  '   steering.stop()   EXIT to its front cog (<= 20 ms), cogstop() and two motor stop()s
  '   steering.driveAtPower() posts one request and waits for the front cog's answer, bounded by
  '                     REQ_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS (20 ms); the synchronized drive's ATN and wait run in the
  '                     front cog (task 3513). No unbounded wait remains (F-6)
  '   steering.getError() -- three hub read-and-clears; no wait
  '   steering.stopMotors() one posted request, <= 20 ms
  '   steering.testGetDriverState(), testGetRawHallTicks(), isStopped() -- hub reads; no wait
  '   wheel start()     as start() above; holdAtStop() one hub write
  '   cogspin()/cogstop() of a spacer -- no wait; beat on every spacer
  '   waitms(PREFLIGHT_MS = 700) the steering and brake-start windows, beat before and after
  ' This file never calls testResetFault() (~2_030 ms worst case, the scan's longest gap).
  ' The debug baud is the pnut-ts default -- this file does not set one -- so every debug figure
  ' above is bounded at a deliberately slow 115_200 baud (the real rate is UNVERIFIED here).
  ' Longest legitimate gap: steering.start() at <= 1_500 ms; next is start() at <= 1_250 ms, then the
  ' 700 ms PREFLIGHT_MS windows. WD_STALL_MS = 4_000 ms clears 1_500 ms by 2_500 ms (2.7x) and is 16x WD_POLL_MS. The watchdog times a gap from the poll at which it SAW the last change, up to
  ' WD_POLL_MS after the real beat, so a legitimate gap always measures shorter than it was and
  ' cannot cross the bound; a real stall's since_ms reads low by up to WD_POLL_MS.
    WD_POLL_MS  = 250                                       ' watchdog sample cadence
    WD_STALL_MS = 4_000                                     ' declare a stall at or above this many ms
    WD_IDLE_MS  = 1_000                                     ' idle-forever chunk, far under WAITMS_MAX_MS

  ' Stack, counted per p2kbAppNoteP2an006SizingCogTaskStacks the way test_bench_scan.spin2 counts
  ' it (params + returns + locals of every frame on the stack at once). The stall path cannot be
  ' exercised off the bench, so it is counted, not measured. Deepest chain, any BC-WATCHDOG
  ' numeric field:
  '   watchdog()        0 params + 0 returns + 3 locals                        =  3
  '   declareStall()    1 param  + 0 returns + 0 locals                        =  1
  '   emitWatchdog()    1 param  + 0 returns + 1 local                         =  2
  '   wdLog.numField()  3 params + 0 returns + 0 locals                        =  3
  '   (isp_bench_log's own, PL-53 -- the same frames the retired wd* copies had:)
  '   lineField()       2 params + 0 returns + 0 locals                        =  2
  '   lineAddNum()      1 param  + 0 returns + 14 locals (digitStack[11] + 3)  = 15
  '   lineAddChar()     1 param  + 0 returns + 0 locals                        =  1
  '                                                                     total  = 27 longs
  ' Every other chain is shallower: BC-WATCHDOG2 and BC-END numeric fields 25 (emitWatchdog2()
  ' and wdEmitEnd() have no locals: the stall values live in the wdSnap* DAT longs, not on the
  ' stack), wdSnapshot() -> testGetTelemetry() 3+1+1+8 = 13, wheelL.stop() under 10.
  ' Task 3521 phase D: declareStall() -> steering.stop() (0) -> rtWheel.stop() (0) ->
  ' bHoldsPinBaseClaim() (1 return) = 3+1+0+0+1 = 5. The deepest chain is unchanged at 27.
  ' The count leaves out the interpreter's per-call bookkeeping and expression scratch, which is
  ' not visible in this repo (UNVERIFIED); even at a generous 8 longs for each of the chain's 7
  ' calls, 27 + 56 = 83 < 128. WD_STACK_LONGS = 128 is the app note's own starting point, used
  ' unshrunk because nothing here was measured. wdStackSentinel abuts the stack; BC-WATCHDOG's
  ' last field reports it, read after that record's own deepest chain has already run.
    WD_STACK_LONGS    = 128
    WD_STACK_SENTINEL = $5A5A_5A5A                          ' set before cogspin, checked in BC-WATCHDOG
    WD_NO_HOLD        = -1                                  ' wdHoldIdx outside any hold: banner, preflight, end

  ' Snapshot slots for the two wheels:
  '  WD_SLOT_LEFT  - wheelL
  '  WD_SLOT_RIGHT - wheelR
    #0, WD_SLOT_LEFT, WD_SLOT_RIGHT
    WD_SLOTS = WD_SLOT_RIGHT + 1

OBJ { objects under test }

#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    user   : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench"              ' banner cfg_id only -- see CON { bench target }
#else
    user   : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig"
#endif
    wheelL : "isp_bldc_motor"                                ' left wheel instance
    wheelR : "isp_bldc_motor"                                ' right wheel instance
    steering : "isp_steering_2wheel"                        ' task 3521 phase D: two-wheel object under test; never running while wheelL/wheelR are (PL-18)
    benchLog : "isp_bench_log"                              ' the record builder (PL-53) and the cog-event quiet window (PL-41, PL-85)
    wdLog    : "isp_bench_log"                              ' the watchdog cog's own record builder: cog 0 may be stalled mid-record in benchLog

DAT { watchdog heartbeat contract, task 3521 phase B -- cog 0 writes these, the watchdog cog reads them }

wdHeartbeat     LONG    0                                   ' beat() adds 1 on every call
wdCheckpoint    LONG    CP_MAIN_INIT                        ' beat()'s last CP_* id
wdDeclaring     LONG    FALSE                               ' the watchdog sets TRUE as declareStall()'s first act
wdHoldIdx       LONG    WD_NO_HOLD                          ' HOLD_* measureHold() is in; WD_NO_HOLD outside a hold
wdSide          LONG    SIDE_NONE                           ' SIDE_* cog 0 is driving (preflight pass or hold)

DAT { watchdog stall snapshot -- written only by the watchdog cog, only after it declares a stall }

wdSnapCheckpoint LONG   CP_MAIN_INIT
wdSnapHoldIdx   LONG    WD_NO_HOLD
wdSnapSide      LONG    SIDE_NONE
wdSnapResult    LONG    RES_NOT_RUN
wdSnapHoldsRun  LONG    0
wdSnapMotorCog  LONG    0[WD_SLOTS]                         ' testGetMotorCog(): cog id + 1, 0 when not running
wdSnapDrvState  LONG    0[WD_SLOTS]                         ' getDriverState(): DCS_*
wdSnapFault     LONG    0[WD_SLOTS]                         ' isFaultSignal(): TRUE/FALSE
wdSnapDuty      LONG    0[WD_SLOTS]                         ' testGetTelemetry() duty
wdSnapErr       LONG    0[WD_SLOTS]                         ' testGetTelemetry() err
wdSnapSenseI    LONG    0[WD_SLOTS]                         ' testGetTelemetry() sense_i_mV
wdSnapTicks     LONG    0[WD_SLOTS]                         ' getRawHallTicks()

DAT { token strings }

sNa             BYTE    "NA", 0
sTrue           BYTE    "TRUE", 0

sMotNone        BYTE    "NONE", 0
sMotLeft        BYTE    "LEFT", 0
sMotRight       BYTE    "RIGHT", 0

sRobotNone      BYTE    "NONE", 0
sRobotFwd       BYTE    "FWD", 0
sRobotRev       BYTE    "REV", 0

sRungZero       BYTE    "ZERO", 0
sRungQtr        BYTE    "QTR", 0
sRungHalf       BYTE    "HALF", 0

sSteadyRamped   BYTE    "RAMPED", 0
sSteadyTimeout  BYTE    "TIMEOUT", 0
sSteadyZerocmd  BYTE    "ZEROCMD", 0

sResOk          BYTE    "OK", 0
sResNotRun      BYTE    "NOT_RUN", 0
sResNoCog       BYTE    "NO_COG", 0
sResReadyTo     BYTE    "READY_TIMEOUT", 0
sResSteadyTo    BYTE    "STEADY_TIMEOUT", 0
sResFault       BYTE    "FAULT", 0
sResStopTo      BYTE    "STOP_TIMEOUT", 0

sCfgBench       BYTE    "BENCH", 0
sCfgUser        BYTE    "USER", 0
sFrameMotor     BYTE    "MOTOR", 0

sBoardRevA      BYTE    "REV_A", 0
sBoardRevB      BYTE    "REV_B", 0
sBoardUnknown   BYTE    "UNKNOWN", 0

sExitComplete   BYTE    "COMPLETE", 0
sExitAborted    BYTE    "ABORTED", 0
sExitWatchdog   BYTE    "WATCHDOG", 0

DAT { sign-off tokens, task 3521 phase C -- each within its TOKMAX_* }

sSfBinChar      BYTE    "CHAR", 0
sSfTaskIscale   BYTE    "3500", 0                           ' R2-CHAR-ISCALE: board detection
sSfTaskInteg    BYTE    "3501", 0                           ' R3-CHAR-INTEG: hall integrity counters
sSfTaskRpm      BYTE    "3502", 0                           ' R4-CHAR-RPM: live rpm
sSfTaskSense    BYTE    "3503", 0                           ' R5-CHAR-SENSE: S-3 ADC scale
sSfCellSense    BYTE    "R5-CHAR-SENSE", 0
sSfCellRpm      BYTE    "R4-CHAR-RPM", 0
sSfCellIscale   BYTE    "R2-CHAR-ISCALE", 0
sSfCellInteg    BYTE    "R3-CHAR-INTEG", 0
sSfCritSense    BYTE    "NET_VS_PASS1_PCT", 0
sSfCritRpm      BYTE    "RPM_ERR", 0
sSfCritIscale   BYTE    "RSENSE_IMPLIED", 0
sSfCritInteg    BYTE    "MISSED_ILLEGAL_SUM", 0
sSfUnitsPct     BYTE    "PCT_X10", 0
sSfUnitsRpm     BYTE    "RPM", 0
sSfUnitsCount   BYTE    "COUNT", 0
sSfPass         BYTE    "PASS", 0
sSfFail         BYTE    "FAIL", 0
sSfNomeas       BYTE    "NOMEAS", 0

DAT { sign-off and record tokens, task 3521 phase D -- each within its TOKMAX_* }

sSfTaskSteer    BYTE    "3533", 0                           ' R10-CHAR-STEER*: PL-28, PL-22 and PL-9
sSfTaskBrake    BYTE    "3535", 0                           ' R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART: commit b34e109, the task 3535 review fix
sSfCellSteerFail  BYTE  "R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL", 0
sSfCellSteerStart BYTE  "R10-CHAR-STEERSTART", 0
sSfCellSteerLive  BYTE  "R10-CHAR-STEERLIVE", 0
sSfCellBrake    BYTE    "R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART", 0
sSfCritNoLeak   BYTE    "RET_NEG_NOLEAK", 0
sSfCritStartCog BYTE    "STEER_START_COG", 0
sSfCritTicks    BYTE    "WHEEL_TICKS", 0
sSfCritBrake    BYTE    "BRAKE_START_MOVE", 0
sSfTaskErr      BYTE    "3555", 0                           ' R16-CHAR-STEERERR: the steering error contract
sSfCellSteerErr BYTE    "R16-CHAR-STEERERR", 0
sSfCritWheel    BYTE    "WHEEL_NAMED", 0
sSfUnitsTicks   BYTE    "TICKS", 0
sSfUnitsBool    BYTE    "BOOL", 0

DAT { Pass 1 meter current per hold, task 3521 phase C -- index HOLD_*, milliamps }

' Each value is the meter mean for one Pass 1 hold (CHAR-RUN-EVALUATION.md, Readings table), placed
' on THIS file's hold by MOTOR and SIGNED MOTOR INCREMENT as the Pass 1 log's BC-HOLD record gives
' them (DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-09-12/debug_260912-153807.log) -- never by caption (Pass 1's
' captions named robot frame while it drove motor frame, PL-19) and never by position. 0 means no
' Pass 1 value, which makes that hold's R5-CHAR-SENSE instance NOMEAS permanently. Cross-check,
' MEASURED in scan run 5 at default offsets (design sec A.5-d): the negative increment is the
' high-current direction on both motors, so both values under 0.6 A sit on positive quarter holds.
pass1HoldMilliAmps  LONG    0                               ' HOLD_ZERO: quiescent, no motion current to compare
                    LONG    536                             ' HOLD_L_FWD_QTR  <- log:476  BC-HOLD hold 1 motor LEFT  cmd_incre  36_750_000, meter 0.536 A
                    LONG    1_054                           ' HOLD_L_REV_QTR  <- log:864  BC-HOLD hold 2 motor LEFT  cmd_incre -36_750_000, meter 1.054 A
                    LONG    570                             ' HOLD_R_FWD_QTR  <- log:1265 BC-HOLD hold 3 motor RIGHT cmd_incre  36_750_000, meter 0.570 A
                    LONG    1_058                           ' HOLD_R_REV_QTR  <- log:1656 BC-HOLD hold 4 motor RIGHT cmd_incre -36_750_000, meter 1.058 A
                    LONG    3_004                           ' HOLD_L_FWD_HALF <- log:2074 BC-HOLD hold 5 motor LEFT  cmd_incre  73_500_000, meter 3.004 A
                    LONG    5_564                           ' HOLD_L_REV_HALF <- log:2464 BC-HOLD hold 6 motor LEFT  cmd_incre -73_500_000, meter 5.564 A
                    LONG    3_140                           ' HOLD_R_FWD_HALF <- log:2869 BC-HOLD hold 7 motor RIGHT cmd_incre  73_500_000, meter 3.140 A
                    LONG    5_530                           ' HOLD_R_REV_HALF <- log:3258 BC-HOLD hold 8 motor RIGHT cmd_incre -73_500_000, meter 5.530 A

DAT { checkpoint tokens, task 3521 phase B -- one per CP_* in checkpointToken(), each at most TOKMAX_CP }

sCpMainInit     BYTE    "MAIN_INIT", 0
sCpMainBanner   BYTE    "MAIN_BANR", 0
sCpMainPlan     BYTE    "MAIN_PLAN", 0
sCpMainRun      BYTE    "MAIN_RUN", 0
sCpMainShutdown BYTE    "MAIN_SHTDN", 0
sCpMainEnd      BYTE    "MAIN_END", 0
sCpPreLeft      BYTE    "PRE_LEFT", 0
sCpPreRight     BYTE    "PRE_RIGHT", 0
sCpHold         BYTE    "HOLD", 0
sCpStartSide    BYTE    "STARTSIDE", 0
sCpLibStart     BYTE    "LIB_START", 0
sCpWaitReady    BYTE    "WAITREADY", 0
sCpLibSense     BYTE    "LIB_SENSE", 0
sCpZero         BYTE    "ZERO", 0
sCpLibCommand   BYTE    "LIB_CMD", 0
sCpAtSpeed      BYTE    "ATSPEED", 0
sCpSteady       BYTE    "STEADY", 0
sCpSettle       BYTE    "SETTLE", 0
sCpWindow       BYTE    "WINDOW", 0
sCpWaitStop     BYTE    "WAITSTOP", 0
sCpStopLeft     BYTE    "STOP_LEFT", 0
sCpStopRight    BYTE    "STOP_RIGHT", 0
sCpLibInteg     BYTE    "LIB_INTEG", 0
sCpLibDrvState  BYTE    "LIB_DRVST", 0
sCpLibCogUp     BYTE    "LIB_COGUP", 0
sCpLibIsReady   BYTE    "LIB_ISRDY", 0
sCpLibIsStopped BYTE    "LIB_ISSTOP", 0
sCpLibTelemetry BYTE    "LIB_TELEM", 0
sCpLibCurrent   BYTE    "LIB_CURR", 0
sCpLibTicks     BYTE    "LIB_TICKS", 0
sCpLibOffsets   BYTE    "LIB_GETOFS", 0
sCpLibRpm       BYTE    "LIB_RPM", 0
sCpLibBoardType BYTE    "LIB_BRDTYP", 0
sCpLibConstants BYTE    "LIB_CONST", 0
sCpEmit         BYTE    "EMIT", 0
sCpNote         BYTE    "NOTE", 0
sCpSteer        BYTE    "STEER", 0
sCpSpacerLoop   BYTE    "SPACERS", 0
sCpSteerStart   BYTE    "STR_START", 0
sCpSteerReady   BYTE    "STR_READY", 0
sCpSteerDrive   BYTE    "STR_DRIVE", 0
sCpSteerStop    BYTE    "STR_STOP", 0
sCpSteerStopWt  BYTE    "STR_STOPWT", 0
sCpSteerRead    BYTE    "STR_READ", 0
sCpBrake        BYTE    "BRAKE", 0
sCpBrakeStart   BYTE    "BRK_START", 0
sCpHoldAtStop   BYTE    "BRK_HOLD", 0
sCpBrakeSettle  BYTE    "BRK_SETTLE", 0
sCpBrakeDrive   BYTE    "BRK_DRIVE", 0
sCpSteerError   BYTE    "STR_ERROR", 0
sCpUnknown      BYTE    "UNKNOWN", 0

DAT { hold caption strings -- every caption names its frame (PL-19) }

sHold0Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 1 of 9 - QUIESCENT ZERO - LEFT MOTOR STARTED AT ZERO COMMAND (motor frame)", 0
sHold1Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 2 of 9 - LEFT MOTOR + INCREMENT 1/4 SPEED (motor frame, robot forward)", 0
sHold2Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 3 of 9 - LEFT MOTOR - INCREMENT 1/4 SPEED (motor frame, robot reverse)", 0
sHold3Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 4 of 9 - RIGHT MOTOR + INCREMENT 1/4 SPEED (motor frame, robot reverse)", 0
sHold4Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 5 of 9 - RIGHT MOTOR - INCREMENT 1/4 SPEED (motor frame, robot forward)", 0
sHold5Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 6 of 9 - LEFT MOTOR + INCREMENT 1/2 SPEED (motor frame, robot forward)", 0
sHold6Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 7 of 9 - LEFT MOTOR - INCREMENT 1/2 SPEED (motor frame, robot reverse)", 0
sHold7Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 8 of 9 - RIGHT MOTOR + INCREMENT 1/2 SPEED (motor frame, robot reverse)", 0
sHold8Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 9 of 9 - RIGHT MOTOR - INCREMENT 1/2 SPEED (motor frame, robot forward)", 0

VAR { run-wide state }

    LONG    bRunReturned                                    ' TRUE once bRunSession() reached its end
    LONG    bPreflightOk                                    ' TRUE when both wheels turned in preflight
    LONG    holdsRun                                        ' holds measured so far

VAR { overflow-proof running means, index ACC_* }

    LONG    accMean[ACC_SLOTS]                              ' floor(sum / count)
    LONG    accRem[ACC_SLOTS]                               ' sum - accMean * count, 0 <= rem < count
    LONG    accCount[ACC_SLOTS]                             ' samples added

VAR { per-hold results, index HOLD_* -- the seam a later sign-off emitter reads }

    LONG    holdResultCode[HOLD_COUNT]                      ' RES_*
    LONG    holdIncre[HOLD_COUNT]                           ' signed motor increment commanded
    LONG    bHoldStarted[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' TRUE when start() gave a cog that reported ready
    LONG    holdStartCog[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' start()'s return
    LONG    holdSenseCog[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' startSenseCog()'s return
    LONG    holdBoardRev[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' REV_* recorded at start
    LONG    holdDeadGap[HOLD_COUNT]                         ' testGetDriveConstants() deadGap
    LONG    holdPwmLimit[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdDutyMin[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdDutyMax[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdAdcFrame[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdFrameCnt[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    bHoldAtSpeed[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' TRUE when DCS_AT_SPEED was seen
    LONG    holdSteadyMs[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' ms from command to AT_SPEED
    LONG    holdSteadySrc[HOLD_COUNT]                       ' pointer to RAMPED / TIMEOUT / ZEROCMD, 0 when not run
    LONG    holdSteadyRate[HOLD_COUNT]                      ' waitForSteady()'s hall-rate at its declaration
    LONG    bHoldStopped[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' TRUE when STOPPED was seen after the zero command
    LONG    holdZeroSamples[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdZeroX10[HOLD_COUNT]                         ' same-lifetime zero, mV x10
    LONG    holdSamples[HOLD_COUNT]                         ' window samples
    LONG    holdWinMs[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdRawX10[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' window sense mean, mV x10
    LONG    holdNetX10[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' raw minus the same-lifetime zero, mV x10
    LONG    holdAmpsMean[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' getCurrent() amps x 10_000, window mean
    LONG    bHoldMotionValid[HOLD_COUNT]                    ' TRUE when the window ran and the cog was up at its end
    LONG    holdRpm[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdTicks[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdRateX10[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdNegDeg[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' testGetFwdRevIndep() fwd (negative increments)
    LONG    holdPosDeg[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' testGetFwdRevIndep() rev (positive increments)
    LONG    holdDutyMean[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdErrMean[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    bHoldIntegValid[HOLD_COUNT]                     ' TRUE when the counts were read from a running cog
    LONG    holdMissed[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' hall missed transitions since this hold's start
    LONG    holdIllegal[HOLD_COUNT]                         ' illegal hall codes since this hold's start
    LONG    holdDrvState[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' DCS_* after the stop wait

VAR { watchdog cog, task 3521 phase B }

    LONG    wdStack[WD_STACK_LONGS]
    LONG    wdStackSentinel                                 ' MUST abut wdStack in this same block: set to
                                                            ' WD_STACK_SENTINEL before cogspin, reported by
                                                            ' BC-WATCHDOG -- cogspin does not detect an overrun
    LONG    wdCogId                                         ' cogspin()'s return; negative when it failed

VAR { steering and brake-start phase state, task 3521 phase D -- the seam emitPhaseDSignoffs() reads }

    LONG    spacerCog[SPACER_MAX]                           ' cogspin() ids of the running spacer cogs
    LONG    spacerStack[SPACER_MAX * SPACER_STACK_LONGS]    ' one SPACER_STACK_LONGS stack per spacer

' Every library call in this phase is UNTRAPPED: since the error contract (tasks 3554/3555) nothing
' in the library aborts, and a refused pin claim returns -1 with ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE. A genuine
' abort is still caught by main()'s single top-level trap around \bRunSession(), whose value is
' printed on every run (P3).

    LONG    bSteerFailCounted                               ' TRUE once the baseline free-cog count was taken
    LONG    bSteerFailAttempted                             ' TRUE when steering.start() was called with spacers holding cogs
    LONG    bSteerFailMeasured                              ' TRUE when that start ran with exactly one free cog
    LONG    steerFailBaseline                               ' free cogs before
    LONG    steerFailSpacers                                ' spacers started to leave one cog free
    LONG    steerFailReturn                                 ' steering.start()'s return with one free cog
    LONG    steerFailFreeAfter                              ' free cogs after the spacers were released
    LONG    bSteerFailClaimsFree                            ' TRUE when this file's wheels then claimed both bench bases (PL-36)
    LONG    steerFailError                                  ' R16-CHAR-STEERERR: steering.getError()'s own result after the failed start
    LONG    steerFailLtError                                ' its left-wheel result
    LONG    steerFailRtError                                ' its right-wheel result
    LONG    bSteerStartRan                                  ' TRUE when the normal steering.start() was called
    LONG    steerStartReturn                                ' its return
    LONG    bSteerBothReady                                 ' TRUE when both wheels left DCS_Unknown within READY_TIMEOUT_MS
    LONG    bSteerLiveRan                                   ' TRUE when the PREFLIGHT_MS tick window ran
    LONG    bSteerDriveDone                                 ' TRUE when driveAtPower() returned TRUE (P5: reported on its own, not folded into "abort")
    LONG    steerLtState                                    ' left wheel DCS_* read just after the window's second tick read
    LONG    steerRtState                                    ' right wheel DCS_* read just after the window's second tick read
    LONG    steerLtTicksDelta                               ' |left raw hall ticks after - before|, clamped to LIM_SMALL
    LONG    steerRtTicksDelta                               ' |right raw hall ticks after - before|, clamped to LIM_SMALL
    LONG    bSteerStopped                                   ' TRUE when both wheels reported STOPPED after stopMotors()

    LONG    bBrakeSteerClear                                ' TRUE when both steering wheels read DCS_Unknown before the brake phase
    LONG    bBrakeRan[BRAKE_COUNT]                          ' TRUE when the instance was reached
    LONG    brakeStartRet[BRAKE_COUNT]                      ' start()'s return
    LONG    bBrakeStarted[BRAKE_COUNT]                      ' TRUE when start() returned the cog testGetMotorCog() reports
    LONG    bBrakeReady[BRAKE_COUNT]                        ' TRUE when the released driver reported ready
    LONG    brakeTicksDelta[BRAKE_COUNT]                    ' signed raw hall-tick delta over the window, clamped to LIM_SMALL
    LONG    bBrakeFaultRead[BRAKE_COUNT]                    ' TRUE when the fault state was read from a running driver
    LONG    bBrakeFault[BRAKE_COUNT]                        ' TRUE when the fault latch or DCS_FAULTED was seen
    LONG    bBrakeStopped[BRAKE_COUNT]                      ' TRUE when STOPPED was seen after the zero command

PUB main() | trapCode, bWdStarted
'' Run the unattended characterisation under a watchdog: watchdog start, banner, preflight, every
'' hold, then stop both wheels and end the session. This is the one exit path, unless the watchdog
'' declares a stall -- then the watchdog cog ends the session and this cog does nothing further.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local trapCode - value delivered by the abort trap around bRunSession()
' @local bWdStarted - TRUE when cogspin() gave the watchdog a cog id 0..MAX_COG_ID

    wdStackSentinel := WD_STACK_SENTINEL                    ' in place BEFORE the cog that could overrun it starts
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    wdCogId := cogspin(NEWCOG, watchdog(), @wdStack)        ' task 3521 phase B: watch cog 0 from here on
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    bWdStarted := (wdCogId >= 0) and (wdCogId <= MAX_COG_ID)
    beat(CP_MAIN_INIT)
    emitWatchdogStart(bWdStarted, wdCogId)
    if bWdStarted == FALSE
        beat(CP_NOTE)
        debug("! WATCHDOG DID NOT START -- this run proceeds UNWATCHED: a stall will be neither named nor stopped")
        beat(CP_NOTE)
    initRun()
    beat(CP_MAIN_BANNER)
    emitBanner()
    beat(CP_MAIN_PLAN)
    emitPlan()
    emitSignoffDecls()                                      ' task 3521 phase C: declare every judged cell before anything moves
    beat(CP_MAIN_RUN)
    bRunReturned := FALSE
    trapCode := \bRunSession()                               ' a library abort lands here, not past the stop()s
    beat(CP_MAIN_SHUTDOWN)
    ' The watchdog is stopped BEFORE the stop()s and BC-END: once main() is past its last record
    ' cog 0 goes silent, and a still-running watchdog would count that silence toward WD_STALL_MS
    ' and emit a bogus second BC-END and marker. wdDeclaring guards the other order: if it is
    ' already TRUE the watchdog owns the session's end, so this cog must neither stop that cog
    ' mid-record nor emit a second BC-END of its own. The beat just above makes the watchdog's
    ' last-seen change fresh, so it cannot newly reach WD_STALL_MS between the test and cogstop()
    ' -- except when cog 0 had itself just come back from a gap of about WD_STALL_MS that the
    ' watchdog was already declaring; that residual race is not closed here (it would need a
    ' lock), and it is the same one test_bench_scan.spin2 carries.
    if wdDeclaring == FALSE
        if bWdStarted
            benchLog.cogEventBegin()
            cogstop(wdCogId)
        shutdownMotors()                                    ' EVERY non-watchdog path: both wheels stop()
        steerStop()                                         ' task 3521 phase D: and the steering object's two, if an abort left them running
        beat(CP_MAIN_END)
        emitSignoffs()                                      ' task 3521 phase C: every declared cell's instances, after the wheels stopped
        emitEnd(trapCode)
        beat(CP_NOTE)
        debug("* BENCH CHAR RUN COMPLETE -- safe to disconnect")
        ' QUOTED, not backticked -- a backtick makes it a display command and the marker is missed.
        debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
        beat(CP_NOTE)
    else
        ' A repeat of WD_IDLE_MS, never one long waitms(): see WAITMS_MAX_MS.
        repeat
            waitms(WD_IDLE_MS)

PRI initRun() | holdIdx
' Reset run-wide state and mark every hold not run.
'
' @local holdIdx - HOLD_* index

    bRunReturned := FALSE
    bPreflightOk := FALSE
    holdsRun := 0
    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_ZERO to HOLD_COUNT - 1
        beat(CP_MAIN_INIT)
        clearHold(holdIdx)
        holdResultCode[holdIdx] := RES_NOT_RUN
    initPhaseD()

PRI bRunSession() : bCompleted
' Preflight, then every configured hold, then the steering and brake-start phases (task 3521
' phase D). A preflight miss skips all three.
'
' @returns bCompleted - TRUE when every configured hold ran

    bCompleted := FALSE
    bPreflightOk := bPreflightWheels()
    if bPreflightOk
        runAllHolds()
        bCompleted := TRUE
        runSteeringPhase()
        runBrakeStartPhase()
    else
        beat(CP_NOTE)
        debug("! SKIPPING HOLDS -- see BC-PREFLIGHT above. Fix the wiring or the declared pin group,")
        debug("!   then re-run. Running nine holds against a wheel that cannot turn wastes the session.")
        beat(CP_NOTE)
    bRunReturned := TRUE

PRI bPreflightWheels() : bOk | side, startedCog, bReady, ticksBefore, ticksAfter, ticksMoved, bStopped, cpPreflight
' Prove each declared wheel can actually turn before committing the session to nine holds.
' Motion, not getBoardType(), is the check: detection is under investigation this sprint. On
' 2026-09-11 the bench config named a pin group with no board on it, and nine holds ran on it.
'
' @returns bOk - TRUE when both declared wheels moved
'
' @local side - SIDE_LEFT then SIDE_RIGHT
' @local startedCog - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reported ready
' @local ticksBefore - hall ticks before the nudge
' @local ticksAfter - hall ticks after the nudge
' @local ticksMoved - signed tick delta across the nudge
' @local bStopped - TRUE when STOPPED was seen after the nudge
' @local cpPreflight - CP_PREFLIGHT_LEFT or CP_PREFLIGHT_RIGHT for this pass

    bOk := TRUE
    repeat side from SIDE_LEFT to SIDE_RIGHT
        cpPreflight := (side == SIDE_RIGHT) ? CP_PREFLIGHT_RIGHT : CP_PREFLIGHT_LEFT
        wdHoldIdx := WD_NO_HOLD
        wdSide := side
        beat(cpPreflight)
        ticksMoved := 0
        bStopped := FALSE
        startedCog, bReady := startSide(side)
        if bReady
            ticksBefore := wheelTicks(side)
            commandMotor(side, PREFLIGHT_INCRE)
            beat(cpPreflight)
            waitms(PREFLIGHT_MS)                            ' the longest legitimate gap without a beat: see WD_STALL_MS
            beat(cpPreflight)
            ticksAfter := wheelTicks(side)
            commandMotor(side, 0)
            bStopped := bWaitStoppedFor(side)
            ticksMoved := ticksAfter - ticksBefore
        shutdownMotors()
        emitPreflight(side, startedCog, ticksMoved, bStopped)
        if ticksMoved == 0
            bOk := FALSE
            beat(CP_NOTE)
            debug("!  wheel on that pin group did NOT turn -- wrong pin group, or wiring, or a dead board")
            beat(CP_NOTE)

PRI runAllHolds() | holdIdx
' Run every configured hold in sequence, quiescent zero through HOLD_LAST, printing each after
' its wheel has stopped.
'
' @local holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold currently running

    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_ZERO to HOLD_LAST
        beat(CP_HOLD)
        measureHold(holdIdx)
        holdsRun += 1
        beat(CP_HOLD)
        emitHoldRecords(holdIdx)

PRI holdInfo(holdIdx) : side, sign, speedIncre, pCaption, pRobotTok, pRungTok
' Return the fixed description of one hold -- the single source of truth for the sequence.
' Motor frame throughout: LEFT + increment is robot forward, RIGHT + increment is robot reverse.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier to describe
' @returns side - SIDE_* the hold drives
' @returns sign - +1 positive increment, -1 negative increment, 0 for the quiescent hold
' @returns speedIncre - unsigned motor-increment magnitude for this hold's rung
' @returns pCaption - pointer to this hold's caption text
' @returns pRobotTok - pointer to the robot-frame direction token (FWD / REV / NONE)
' @returns pRungTok - pointer to this hold's speed-rung token

    case holdIdx
        HOLD_ZERO:
            side := HOLD_ZERO_SIDE
            sign := 0
            speedIncre := 0
            pCaption := @sHold0Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotNone
            pRungTok := @sRungZero
        HOLD_L_FWD_QTR:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold1Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_L_REV_QTR:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold2Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotRev
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_R_FWD_QTR:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold3Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotRev
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_R_REV_QTR:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold4Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_L_FWD_HALF:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold5Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        HOLD_L_REV_HALF:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold6Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotRev
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        HOLD_R_FWD_HALF:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold7Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotRev
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        other:                                               ' HOLD_R_REV_HALF
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold8Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf

PRI measureHold(holdIdx) | side, sign, speedIncre, motorIncre, bWindowGo, steadyTok, steadyMs, steadyRate
' Measure one hold end to end into the per-hold VAR longs; prints nothing. Steps: start the
' hold's wheel with the other wheel not running, same-lifetime zero, command, AT_SPEED, rate
' check, settle, window, zero command, stop wait, read integrity counts, stop the wheel.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold to measure
'
' @local side - SIDE_* the hold drives
' @local sign - +1, -1, or 0 for the quiescent hold
' @local speedIncre - unsigned increment magnitude
' @local motorIncre - signed increment commanded (sign * speedIncre)
' @local bWindowGo - TRUE when the sample window may run
' @local steadyTok - waitForSteady()'s source token
' @local steadyMs - waitForSteady()'s elapsed ms (not recorded; AT_SPEED time is)
' @local steadyRate - waitForSteady()'s hall rate at its declaration

    side, sign, speedIncre, _, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    wdHoldIdx := holdIdx                                    ' for the watchdog: which hold, which wheel
    wdSide := side
    beat(CP_HOLD)
    clearHold(holdIdx)
    motorIncre := sign * speedIncre
    holdIncre[holdIdx] := motorIncre
    bWindowGo := FALSE
    startHoldWheel(holdIdx, side)
    if bHoldStarted[holdIdx]
        measureZero(holdIdx, side)
        if motorIncre == 0
            steadyTok, steadyMs, steadyRate := waitForSteady(side, 0)
            holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] := steadyTok
            holdSteadyRate[holdIdx] := steadyRate
            bWindowGo := (holdResultCode[holdIdx] == RES_OK)
        elseif holdResultCode[holdIdx] == RES_OK
            commandMotor(side, motorIncre)
            if bWaitAtSpeed(holdIdx, side)
                steadyTok, steadyMs, steadyRate := waitForSteady(side, motorIncre)
                holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] := steadyTok
                holdSteadyRate[holdIdx] := steadyRate
                ' a rate-check timeout is recorded as steady_src TIMEOUT, never as the hold's result:
                '  AT_SPEED (the driver's own ramp-complete state) has already been seen, so the hold is
                '  still measured and printed -- but its window cells (SENSE, RPM, ISCALE) are NOMEAS, so a
                '  window that may hold the end of the ramp never passes silently (task 3574). MEASURED:
                '  0 of 24 motion holds timed out across the three char runs (Visits 1, 2 and 4)
                bWindowGo := bSettleHold(holdIdx, side)
        if bWindowGo
            sampleWindow(holdIdx, side)
        if bWheelCogUp(side)
            commandMotor(side, 0)
            bHoldStopped[holdIdx] := bWaitStoppedFor(side)
            if bHoldStopped[holdIdx] == FALSE
                setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_STOP_TIMEOUT)
        if bWheelCogUp(side)
            holdMissed[holdIdx], holdIllegal[holdIdx] := wheelIntegrity(side)
            bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx] := TRUE
            holdDrvState[holdIdx] := wheelDrvState(side)
    shutdownMotors()

PRI clearHold(holdIdx)
' Reset one hold's record to its not-measured state, result OK.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index

    holdResultCode[holdIdx] := RES_OK
    holdIncre[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldStarted[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdStartCog[holdIdx] := -1
    holdSenseCog[holdIdx] := -1
    holdBoardRev[holdIdx] := wheelL.REV_Unknown
    holdDeadGap[holdIdx] := 0
    holdPwmLimit[holdIdx] := 0
    holdDutyMin[holdIdx] := 0
    holdDutyMax[holdIdx] := 0
    holdAdcFrame[holdIdx] := 0
    holdFrameCnt[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldAtSpeed[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdSteadyMs[holdIdx] := 0
    holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] := 0
    holdSteadyRate[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldStopped[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdZeroSamples[holdIdx] := 0
    holdZeroX10[holdIdx] := 0
    holdSamples[holdIdx] := 0
    holdWinMs[holdIdx] := 0
    holdRawX10[holdIdx] := 0
    holdNetX10[holdIdx] := 0
    holdAmpsMean[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldMotionValid[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdRpm[holdIdx] := 0
    holdTicks[holdIdx] := 0
    holdRateX10[holdIdx] := 0
    holdNegDeg[holdIdx] := 0
    holdPosDeg[holdIdx] := 0
    holdDutyMean[holdIdx] := 0
    holdErrMean[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdMissed[holdIdx] := 0
    holdIllegal[holdIdx] := 0
    holdDrvState[holdIdx] := wheelL.DCS_Unknown

PRI setHoldResult(holdIdx, resCode)
' Record a hold result: the first cause is kept, but a fault or a lost cog always overwrites,
' because either one invalidates whatever timeout came before it.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param resCode - RES_* cause

    if (holdResultCode[holdIdx] == RES_OK) or (resCode == RES_FAULT) or (resCode == RES_NO_COG)
        holdResultCode[holdIdx] := resCode

PRI startHoldWheel(holdIdx, side) | startedCog, bReady
' Start the hold's wheel with the other wheel not running, read its front cog id, and record the
' start-time readings: start() return, detected board revision and the drive constants.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
'
' @local startedCog - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reported ready

    startedCog, bReady := startSide(side)
    holdStartCog[holdIdx] := startedCog
    if (startedCog < 0) or (startedCog > MAX_COG_ID)
        setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
    elseif bReady == FALSE
        setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_READY_TIMEOUT)
    else
        bHoldStarted[holdIdx] := TRUE
        holdSenseCog[holdIdx] := wheelStartSense(side)      ' the front cog start() launched, which keeps the rpm window
        holdBoardRev[holdIdx] := wheelBoardRev(side)
        holdDeadGap[holdIdx], holdPwmLimit[holdIdx], holdDutyMin[holdIdx], holdDutyMax[holdIdx], ...
            holdAdcFrame[holdIdx], holdFrameCnt[holdIdx] := wheelDriveConstants(side)

PRI startSide(side) : startedCog, bReady
' Stop both wheels, then start only the named wheel and wait (bounded) for it to report ready.
' stop() on a never-started instance touches no pin (isp_bldc_motor stop() guards its pinclear
' on this instance's own pin claim).
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns startedCog - start()'s return: cog id 0..7, or -1
' @returns bReady - TRUE when the started driver reported ready within READY_TIMEOUT_MS

    beat(CP_START_SIDE)
    shutdownMotors()
    startedCog := -1
    bReady := FALSE
    beat(CP_LIB_START)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startedCog := wheelR.start(RIGHT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    else
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startedCog := wheelL.start(LEFT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    beat(CP_LIB_START)
    if startedCog >= 0
        bReady := bWaitUntilReady(side)

PRI bWaitUntilReady(side) : bReady | startMs
' Wait, bounded by READY_TIMEOUT_MS, for the just-started driver cog to report ready.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bReady - TRUE when ready was seen
'
' @local startMs - getms() when the wait began

    bReady := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        beat(CP_LOOP_WAITREADY)
        if isWheelReady(side)
            bReady := TRUE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= READY_TIMEOUT_MS
            quit
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)

PRI measureZero(holdIdx, side) | sampleIdx, nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault
' Read the current-sense zero at zero command, in this hold's own driver lifetime (PL-32).
' No debug() and no debug-emitting library call inside this loop.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
'
' @local sampleIdx - sample counter
' @local nDuty - duty sample (unused here)
' @local nErr - error sample (unused here)
' @local nSenseI - sense_i_mV sample
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* sample
' @local bDidFault - fault sample

    accReset(ACC_ZERO)
    repeat sampleIdx from 1 to ZERO_SAMPLES
        beat(CP_LOOP_ZERO)                                  ' a call and two hub writes, no wait, no debug(): see beat()
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
        if bWheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
            quit
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
        if bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_FAULT)
            quit
        accAdd(ACC_ZERO, nSenseI)
    holdZeroSamples[holdIdx] := accCount[ACC_ZERO]
    holdZeroX10[holdIdx] := accMeanX10(ACC_ZERO)

PRI bWaitAtSpeed(holdIdx, side) : bAtSpeed | startMs, eDrvrState, bDidFault, nDuty, nErr, nSenseI
' Wait, bounded by ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS, for DCS_AT_SPEED after a motion command.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bAtSpeed - TRUE when AT_SPEED was seen
'
' @local startMs - getms() at the wait start
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* sample
' @local bDidFault - fault sample
' @local nDuty - duty sample (unused here)
' @local nErr - error sample (unused here)
' @local nSenseI - sense sample (unused here)

    bAtSpeed := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        beat(CP_LOOP_ATSPEED)
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
        if bWheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
            quit
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
        if bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_FAULT)
            quit
        if eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_AT_SPEED
            bAtSpeed := TRUE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT)
            quit
    holdSteadyMs[holdIdx] := getms() - startMs
    bHoldAtSpeed[holdIdx] := bAtSpeed

PRI bSettleHold(holdIdx, side) : bSettled | startMs, eDrvrState, bDidFault, nDuty, nErr, nSenseI
' Hold SETTLE_MS at the commanded increment, polling for a fault or a lost cog.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bSettled - TRUE when the settle completed without a fault or lost cog
'
' @local startMs - getms() at settle start
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* sample
' @local bDidFault - fault sample
' @local nDuty - duty sample (unused here)
' @local nErr - error sample (unused here)
' @local nSenseI - sense sample (unused here)

    bSettled := TRUE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        beat(CP_LOOP_SETTLE)
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
        if bWheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
            bSettled := FALSE
            quit
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
        if bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_FAULT)
            bSettled := FALSE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= SETTLE_MS
            quit

PRI sampleWindow(holdIdx, side) | startMs, startTicks, endTicks, nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, ...
    bDidFault, nAmps, rateTicks
' Sample every SAMPLE_MS for WINDOW_MS into the running means, then fill the hold's window
' fields. testGetRpm() is read at the window's end: at least SETTLE_MS + WINDOW_MS after
' AT_SPEED, past the ~1 s the front cog's rpm window needs. No debug() inside the loop, and
' every library call in it (testGetMotorCog, testGetTelemetry, getCurrent) emits none.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
'
' @local startMs - getms() at window start
' @local startTicks - hall ticks at window start
' @local endTicks - hall ticks at window end
' @local nDuty - duty sample
' @local nErr - position-error sample
' @local nSenseI - sense_i_mV sample
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* sample
' @local bDidFault - fault sample
' @local nAmps - getCurrent() amps x 10_000 sample
' @local rateTicks - tick count clamped for the rate arithmetic

    accReset(ACC_SENSE)
    accReset(ACC_AMPS)
    accReset(ACC_DUTY)
    accReset(ACC_ERR)
    startTicks := wheelTicks(side)
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        beat(CP_LOOP_WINDOW)                                ' a call and two hub writes, no wait, no debug(): see beat()
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
        if bWheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
            quit
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
        if bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_FAULT)
            quit
        nAmps := wheelCurrent(side)
        accAdd(ACC_SENSE, nSenseI)
        accAdd(ACC_AMPS, nAmps)
        accAdd(ACC_DUTY, nDuty)
        accAdd(ACC_ERR, nErr)
        if (getms() - startMs) >= WINDOW_MS
            quit
    holdWinMs[holdIdx] := getms() - startMs
    holdSamples[holdIdx] := accCount[ACC_SENSE]
    if accCount[ACC_SENSE] > 0
        holdRawX10[holdIdx] := accMeanX10(ACC_SENSE)
        holdAmpsMean[holdIdx] := accMean[ACC_AMPS]
        holdDutyMean[holdIdx] := accMean[ACC_DUTY]
        holdErrMean[holdIdx] := accMean[ACC_ERR]
        ' both operands are clamped to LIM_BIG first, so the difference is within +/-2e9 < POSX
        holdNetX10[holdIdx] := ((holdRawX10[holdIdx] #> -LIM_BIG) <# LIM_BIG) - ((holdZeroX10[holdIdx] #> -LIM_BIG) <# LIM_BIG)
        if bWheelCogUp(side)
            endTicks := wheelTicks(side)
            holdTicks[holdIdx] := abs(endTicks - startTicks)
            rateTicks := holdTicks[holdIdx] <# RATE_TICKS_CAP
            if holdWinMs[holdIdx] > 0
                holdRateX10[holdIdx] := (rateTicks * RATE_X10_SCALE) / holdWinMs[holdIdx]
            holdRpm[holdIdx] := wheelRpm(side)
            holdNegDeg[holdIdx], holdPosDeg[holdIdx] := wheelOffsets(side)
            bHoldMotionValid[holdIdx] := TRUE

PRI bWaitStoppedFor(side) : bStopped | startMs
' Wait, bounded by STOP_TIMEOUT_MS, for the named wheel's running driver to report STOPPED.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bStopped - TRUE when STOPPED was seen
'
' @local startMs - getms() when the wait began

    bStopped := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        beat(CP_LOOP_WAITSTOP)
        if bWheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            quit
        if isWheelStopped(side)
            bStopped := TRUE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= STOP_TIMEOUT_MS
            quit
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)

PRI waitForSteady(side, cmdIncre) : steadySrcTok, elapsedMs, tickRate | prevPos, curPos, ...
    prevRate, curRate, consecCount, bTimedOut, diffPct
' Declare steady state either instantly (the quiescent-zero hold, ZEROCMD) or once
' STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES consecutive hall-tick-rate samples agree within STEADY_TOL_PCT, or
' at STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS regardless (declare steady anyway, source TIMEOUT).
'
' @param side - SIDE_* under test
' @param cmdIncre - signed motor increment just commanded; 0 selects the ZEROCMD path
' @returns steadySrcTok - pointer to RAMPED / TIMEOUT / ZEROCMD
' @returns elapsedMs - milliseconds from command issue to this steady-state declaration
' @returns tickRate - hall-tick rate observed at the declaration (0 for ZEROCMD)
'
' @local prevPos - hall-tick position at the previous sample
' @local curPos - hall-tick position at the current sample
' @local prevRate - hall-tick rate at the previous sample, -1 before the first sample
' @local curRate - hall-tick rate at the current sample
' @local consecCount - consecutive samples agreeing within STEADY_TOL_PCT
' @local bTimedOut - TRUE once STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS has elapsed without confirmation
' @local diffPct - percent difference between curRate and prevRate

    if cmdIncre == 0
        steadySrcTok := @sSteadyZerocmd
        elapsedMs := 0
        tickRate := 0
    else
        prevPos := wheelTicks(side)
        prevRate := -1
        consecCount := 0
        elapsedMs := 0
        bTimedOut := FALSE
        repeat
            beat(CP_LOOP_STEADY)
            waitms(STEADY_SAMPLE_MS)
            elapsedMs += STEADY_SAMPLE_MS
            curPos := wheelTicks(side)
            curRate := absValue(curPos - prevPos) * (MS_PER_SEC / STEADY_SAMPLE_MS)
            prevPos := curPos
            if prevRate == -1
                consecCount := 1
            elseif prevRate == 0
                consecCount := (curRate == 0) ? consecCount + 1 : 1
            else
                diffPct := (absValue(curRate - prevRate) * 100) / prevRate
                consecCount := (diffPct <= STEADY_TOL_PCT) ? consecCount + 1 : 1
            prevRate := curRate
            bTimedOut := (elapsedMs >= STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS)
        until (consecCount >= STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES) or bTimedOut
        tickRate := curRate
        steadySrcTok := bTimedOut ? @sSteadyTimeout : @sSteadyRamped

PRI absValue(signedVal) : magnitude
' Return the absolute value of a signed number.
'
' @param signedVal - value to make non-negative
' @returns magnitude - |signedVal|

    magnitude := (signedVal < 0) ? (0 - signedVal) : signedVal

PRI accReset(accIdx)
' Empty one running mean.
'
' @param accIdx - ACC_* slot

    accMean[accIdx] := 0
    accRem[accIdx] := 0
    accCount[accIdx] := 0

PRI accAdd(accIdx, sampleVal) | clampedVal, newCount, deltaVal, quotVal, remVal
' Add one sample to a running mean without ever storing the sum (PL-20; bound in the CON block
' above). Floor division is built from truncating / by correcting a negative remainder, so the
' result does not depend on whether / truncates or floors.
'
' @param accIdx - ACC_* slot
' @param sampleVal - the sample
'
' @local clampedVal - sample clamped to +/-ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT
' @local newCount - count including this sample
' @local deltaVal - remainder + sample - mean, |deltaVal| < 1_100_000_000
' @local quotVal - deltaVal / newCount, corrected to a floor
' @local remVal - deltaVal - quotVal * newCount, corrected into 0..newCount-1

    clampedVal := (sampleVal #> (0 - ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT)) <# ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT
    if accCount[accIdx] < ACC_COUNT_CAP
        newCount := accCount[accIdx] + 1
        deltaVal := accRem[accIdx] + clampedVal - accMean[accIdx]
        quotVal := deltaVal / newCount
        remVal := deltaVal - (quotVal * newCount)
        if remVal < 0
            remVal += newCount
            quotVal -= 1
        accMean[accIdx] += quotVal
        accRem[accIdx] := remVal
        accCount[accIdx] := newCount

PRI accMeanX10(accIdx) : meanX10 | boundedMean
' Return a running mean x10, truncated toward negative infinity; 0 when empty.
'
' @param accIdx - ACC_* slot
' @returns meanX10 - mean x10
'
' @local boundedMean - floor mean clamped to +/-ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT so the x10 cannot overflow

    meanX10 := 0
    if accCount[accIdx] > 0
        boundedMean := (accMean[accIdx] #> (0 - ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT)) <# ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT
        meanX10 := (boundedMean * X10) + ((accRem[accIdx] * X10) / accCount[accIdx])

PRI commandMotor(side, motorIncre) | safeIncre
' Command a signed motor increment -- the TESTING USE raw-increment path, never followed by
' stopAfterTime(). Anything beyond DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE is commanded as zero.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @param motorIncre - signed motor increment to drive at
'
' @local safeIncre - increment actually commanded

    safeIncre := motorIncre
    if abs(motorIncre) > DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE
        safeIncre := 0
    beat(CP_LIB_COMMAND)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        wheelR.testDriveAtMotorIncrement(safeIncre)
    elseif side == SIDE_LEFT
        wheelL.testDriveAtMotorIncrement(safeIncre)
    beat(CP_LIB_COMMAND)

PRI shutdownMotors()
' Stop both wheels unconditionally. stop() on a never-started instance touches no pin. Cog 0
' only: it beats. The watchdog calls wheelL.stop()/wheelR.stop() directly instead.

    beat(CP_LIB_STOP_LEFT)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    wheelL.stop()
    beat(CP_LIB_STOP_LEFT)
    beat(CP_LIB_STOP_RIGHT)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    wheelR.stop()
    beat(CP_LIB_STOP_RIGHT)

PRI bWheelCogUp(side) : bRunning
' Report whether the named wheel has a running driver cog (stop() zeroes motorCog).
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bRunning - TRUE when the driver cog is running

    beat(CP_LIB_COGUP)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        bRunning := (wheelR.testGetMotorCog() <> 0)
    else
        bRunning := (wheelL.testGetMotorCog() <> 0)
    beat(CP_LIB_COGUP)

PRI isWheelReady(side) : bReady
' Report whether the named wheel's running driver reports ready.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bReady - TRUE when running and ready

    bReady := FALSE
    if bWheelCogUp(side)
        beat(CP_LIB_ISREADY)
        if side == SIDE_RIGHT
            bReady := wheelR.isReady()
        else
            bReady := wheelL.isReady()
        beat(CP_LIB_ISREADY)

PRI isWheelStopped(side) : bStopped
' Report whether the named wheel's running driver reports STOPPED.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bStopped - TRUE when running and STOPPED

    bStopped := FALSE
    if bWheelCogUp(side)
        beat(CP_LIB_ISSTOPPED)
        if side == SIDE_RIGHT
            bStopped := wheelR.isStopped()
        else
            bStopped := wheelL.isStopped()
        beat(CP_LIB_ISSTOPPED)

PRI wheelDrvState(side) : eDrvrState
' Driver state of the named wheel, DCS_Unknown when no cog is running.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns eDrvrState - DCS_* state

    eDrvrState := wheelL.DCS_Unknown
    if bWheelCogUp(side)
        beat(CP_LIB_DRVSTATE)
        if side == SIDE_RIGHT
            eDrvrState := wheelR.getDriverState()
        else
            eDrvrState := wheelL.getDriverState()
        beat(CP_LIB_DRVSTATE)

PRI wheelTelemetry(side) : nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault
' Snapshot the named wheel's per-cycle driver status. Callers check bWheelCogUp() first (PL-21).
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nDuty - latest duty value
' @returns nErr - latest position-error value
' @returns nSenseI - latest sense_i_mV, true millivolts
' @returns eDrvrState - DCS_* driver state
' @returns bDidFault - TRUE when the driver has faulted

    beat(CP_LIB_TELEMETRY)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, _, _, _, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelR.testGetTelemetry()
    else
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, _, _, _, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelL.testGetTelemetry()
    beat(CP_LIB_TELEMETRY)

PRI wheelCurrent(side) : nAmps
' getCurrent() of the named wheel: amps x 10_000 (0.1 mA units), per its doc comment.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nAmps - current, 0.1 mA units

    beat(CP_LIB_CURRENT)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nAmps, _ := wheelR.getCurrent()
    else
        nAmps, _ := wheelL.getCurrent()
    beat(CP_LIB_CURRENT)

PRI wheelTicks(side) : nTicks
' Raw hall ticks of the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nTicks - hall-tick position

    beat(CP_LIB_TICKS)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nTicks := wheelR.getRawHallTicks()
    else
        nTicks := wheelL.getRawHallTicks()
    beat(CP_LIB_TICKS)

PRI wheelIntegrity(side) : nMissed, nIllegal
' Hall integrity counts of the named wheel since its last start.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nMissed - missed transitions
' @returns nIllegal - illegal hall codes

    beat(CP_LIB_INTEGRITY)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nMissed, nIllegal := wheelR.getHallIntegrityCounts()
    else
        nMissed, nIllegal := wheelL.getHallIntegrityCounts()
    beat(CP_LIB_INTEGRITY)

PRI wheelOffsets(side) : negDeg, posDeg
' Applied commutation offsets of the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns negDeg - offset_fwd degrees (negative increments)
' @returns posDeg - offset_rev degrees (positive increments)

    beat(CP_LIB_OFFSETS)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        negDeg, posDeg := wheelR.testGetFwdRevIndep()
    else
        negDeg, posDeg := wheelL.testGetFwdRevIndep()
    beat(CP_LIB_OFFSETS)

PRI wheelRpm(side) : nRpm
' testGetRpm() of the named wheel (maintained only by its front cog).
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nRpm - rpm over the front cog's ~1 s window

    beat(CP_LIB_RPM)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nRpm := wheelR.testGetRpm()
    else
        nRpm := wheelL.testGetRpm()
    beat(CP_LIB_RPM)

PRI wheelStartSense(side) : senseCog
' startSenseCog() for the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns senseCog - the front cog's cog id 0..7, or -1

    beat(CP_LIB_STARTSENSE)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        senseCog := wheelR.startSenseCog()
    else
        senseCog := wheelL.startSenseCog()
    beat(CP_LIB_STARTSENSE)

PRI wheelBoardRev(side) : eBoardRev
' Board revision of the named wheel; with its driver running this is the revision recorded at start.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns eBoardRev - REV_* value

    beat(CP_LIB_BOARDTYPE)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        eBoardRev := wheelR.getBoardType()
    else
        eBoardRev := wheelL.getBoardType()
    beat(CP_LIB_BOARDTYPE)

PRI wheelDriveConstants(side) : deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt
' testGetDriveConstants() of the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns deadGap - commutation dead-time, system ticks
' @returns pwmLimit - PWM duty hard limit
' @returns dutyMin - minimum duty, 1/16ths
' @returns dutyMax - maximum duty, 1/16ths
' @returns adcFrame - ADC sample period
' @returns frameCnt - PWM frame length, system ticks

    beat(CP_LIB_CONSTANTS)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt := wheelR.testGetDriveConstants()
    else
        deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt := wheelL.testGetDriveConstants()
    beat(CP_LIB_CONSTANTS)

PRI initPhaseD() | brakeIdx
' Mark every phase D measurement not run, so an unreached instance is NOMEAS with n 0.
'
' @local brakeIdx - BRK_* index

    steerFailError := STEERERR_OK_CODE
    steerFailLtError := STEERERR_OK_CODE
    steerFailRtError := STEERERR_OK_CODE
    bSteerFailCounted := FALSE
    bSteerFailAttempted := FALSE
    bSteerFailMeasured := FALSE
    steerFailBaseline := 0
    steerFailSpacers := 0
    steerFailReturn := 0
    steerFailFreeAfter := 0
    bSteerFailClaimsFree := FALSE
    bSteerStartRan := FALSE
    steerStartReturn := 0
    bSteerBothReady := FALSE
    bSteerLiveRan := FALSE
    bSteerDriveDone := FALSE
    steerLtState := steering.DCS_Unknown
    steerRtState := steering.DCS_Unknown
    steerLtTicksDelta := 0
    steerRtTicksDelta := 0
    bSteerStopped := FALSE
    bBrakeSteerClear := FALSE
    repeat brakeIdx from BRK_L_POS to BRAKE_COUNT - 1
        beat(CP_MAIN_INIT)
        bBrakeRan[brakeIdx] := FALSE
        brakeStartRet[brakeIdx] := 0
        bBrakeStarted[brakeIdx] := FALSE
        bBrakeReady[brakeIdx] := FALSE
        brakeTicksDelta[brakeIdx] := 0
        bBrakeFaultRead[brakeIdx] := FALSE
        bBrakeFault[brakeIdx] := FALSE
        bBrakeStopped[brakeIdx] := FALSE

PRI runSteeringPhase() | baseline, spacersStarted, startRet, ltTicksBefore, rtTicksBefore, ltTicksAfter, rtTicksAfter
' The steering-object phase (task 3521 phase D): R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL, R10-CHAR-STEERSTART and
' R10-CHAR-STEERLIVE, then BC-STEER once every wheel is stopped. Prints nothing before that.
'
' ORDER (PL-18): this file's wheelL/wheelR and the steering object's ltWheel/rtWheel share the
' pin-claim registry, so both of this file's wheels are stop()ped first, and the phase ends with
' steering.stop() before runBrakeStartPhase() starts a wheel again.
'
' FREE COGS EXPECTED: 6 -- 8 cogs less cog 0 and the watchdog cog (7 when BC-WDSTART says the
' watchdog did not start). Every hold and preflight pass ends in shutdownMotors(), and a motor
' instance's stop() stops its sense cog as well as its driver cog (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 stop()),
' so no driver or sense cog outlives a hold. That the -d debugger takes no cog of its own is not
' visible in this repo (UNVERIFIED); fail_baseline in BC-STEER records the real count.
'
' STEERFAIL: all but one free cog is occupied, so ltWheel.startOwned() takes the last cog and
' rtWheel.startOwned() fails; start() must stop the left driver and return -1. PASS needs the return
' -1 AND the free-cog count after == baseline (a leaked driver cog reads one short) AND this file's
' own wheelL and wheelR then start on the bench bases (bClaimsFreeCheck(): a failed rtWheel start
' that kept its pin claim, PL-36, refuses wheelR's claim). No cleanup stop() runs between the
' failed start and that check (P6: check before you clean up), so nothing can mask a leaked claim.
' UNFIXED library (before the :124-133 failure path): the failed right start was ignored, the
' left driver cog was never stopped, and the sense-cog start (no cog left) decided the return --
' so free-after = baseline - 1 and the cell FAILs on the leak whatever the return was.
'
' STEERERR (task 3555): right after that failed start, before anything else runs on this cog,
' steering.getError()'s three results are read. PASS needs the right wheel's result to be
' ERR_NO_FREE_COG and the left wheel's NO_ERROR: the caller learns WHICH wheel could not start.
' The steering object's own result is printed, not judged. UNFIXED (before the error contract):
' getError() did not exist, and a failed start reported only -1. NOMEAS when STEERFAIL is.
'
' STEERSTART: a normal start. PASS needs the return in 0..7 AND both wheels leaving DCS_Unknown,
' read through the TEST-USE pass-through testGetDriverState(). No pass-through exposes a wheel's
' motorCog, so driver state is the evidence: init() sets drv_state DCS_Unknown before coginit and
' stop() sets it after cogstop, and only the driver's own status block-write in .ctlMotor changes
' it -- which a sync-started driver reaches only after waitatn has returned. So a state other than
' DCS_Unknown proves that driver cog runs AND was released.
'
' STEERLIVE: raw driver-maintained hall ticks (testGetRawHallTicks(), the driver's pos, rewritten
' by the same block-write every control pass), read before and after a PREFLIGHT_MS window of
' steering.driveAtPower(STEER_POWER, STEER_POWER). The front cog's getRotationCount() total is
' not used: it accumulates abs() deltas, is zeroed by resetTracking(), and getRotationCount()
' prints a debug() line. Liveness at the reads is the driver state just after the second read
' (l_state/r_state). The drive is still commanded only when both wheels reported a state, though
' driveAtPower() is now bounded (task 3513, F-6). NOMEAS only when start() returned outside 0..7 --
' STEERSTART already FAILs that.
'
' Every call here is UNTRAPPED: nothing in the library aborts (tasks 3554/3555). A genuine abort is
' caught by main()'s single top-level trap around \bRunSession() instead.
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before STEERFAIL
' @local spacersStarted - spacers occupying cogs during STEERFAIL
' @local startRet - steering.start()'s return
' @local ltTicksBefore - left raw hall ticks before the window
' @local rtTicksBefore - right raw hall ticks before the window
' @local ltTicksAfter - left raw hall ticks after the window
' @local rtTicksAfter - right raw hall ticks after the window

    wdHoldIdx := WD_NO_HOLD
    wdSide := SIDE_NONE
    beat(CP_STEER)
    shutdownMotors()                                        ' PL-18: release wheelL/wheelR's pin claims before the steering object claims them

    ' (a) R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    steerFailBaseline := baseline
    bSteerFailCounted := TRUE
    if baseline >= STEERFAIL_MIN_BASELINE
        spacersStarted := occupySpacers(baseline - 1)
        steerFailSpacers := spacersStarted
        bSteerFailAttempted := TRUE
        beat(CP_LIB_STEER_START)
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startRet := steering.start(LEFT_TEST_BASE, RIGHT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE, TEST_DET_MODE)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        beat(CP_LIB_STEER_START)
        steerFailReturn := startRet
        beat(CP_LIB_STEER_ERROR)
        steerFailError, steerFailLtError, steerFailRtError := steering.getError()
        beat(CP_LIB_STEER_ERROR)
        releaseSpacers(spacersStarted)
        beat(CP_STEER)
        steerFailFreeAfter := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
        bSteerFailMeasured := (spacersStarted == baseline - 1)
        ' P6 / PL-36: check FIRST, clean up AFTER -- no steerStop() runs before this check, or it
        ' would release a leaked claim and mask exactly the leak this cell exists to catch
        bSteerFailClaimsFree := bClaimsFreeCheck()
        ' only now release whatever the library still holds, so STEERSTART measures its own start
        steerStop()

    ' (b) R10-CHAR-STEERSTART
    beat(CP_STEER)
    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_START)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startRet := steering.start(LEFT_TEST_BASE, RIGHT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE, TEST_DET_MODE)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_START)
    steerStartReturn := startRet
    bSteerStartRan := TRUE
    if (startRet >= 0) and (startRet <= MAX_COG_ID)
        bSteerBothReady := bWaitSteerReady()

        ' (c) R10-CHAR-STEERLIVE
        ltTicksBefore, rtTicksBefore := steerTicks()
        if bSteerBothReady
            beat(CP_STEER_DRIVE)
            steering.driveAtPower(STEER_POWER, STEER_POWER)
            bSteerDriveDone := TRUE
            beat(CP_STEER_DRIVE)
        beat(CP_STEER_DRIVE)
        waitms(PREFLIGHT_MS)                                ' the same increment and duration the 13-tick measurement used
        beat(CP_STEER_DRIVE)
        ltTicksAfter, rtTicksAfter := steerTicks()
        steerLtState, steerRtState := steerStates()
        if bSteerBothReady
            steerStopMotors()
            bSteerStopped := bWaitSteerStopped()
        steerLtTicksDelta := absValue(((ltTicksAfter - ltTicksBefore) #> (0 - LIM_SMALL)) <# LIM_SMALL)
        steerRtTicksDelta := absValue(((rtTicksAfter - rtTicksBefore) #> (0 - LIM_SMALL)) <# LIM_SMALL)
        bSteerLiveRan := TRUE
    steerStop()
    beat(CP_STEER)
    emitSteer()

PRI bClaimsFreeCheck() : bFree | startRet
' R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL's PL-36 limb: start this file's own wheelL and then wheelR on the bench bases
' and require a driver cog id from each, then stop both. A pin group still claimed by another
' instance (a failed steering rtWheel start that kept its claim) makes that wheel's start() return
' -1 with ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE (task 3554: a refused claim no longer aborts), which is this limb's
' FAIL case. Each start commands zero speed, so nothing moves.
'
' @returns bFree - TRUE when both wheels started on their bench bases
'
' @local startRet - start()'s return

    bFree := TRUE
    beat(CP_STEER)
    shutdownMotors()
    startRet := brakeStart(SIDE_LEFT)
    if (startRet < 0) or (startRet > MAX_COG_ID)
        bFree := FALSE
    startRet := brakeStart(SIDE_RIGHT)
    if (startRet < 0) or (startRet > MAX_COG_ID)
        bFree := FALSE
    shutdownMotors()

PRI bWaitSteerReady() : bReady | startMs, eLeftState, eRightState
' Wait, bounded by READY_TIMEOUT_MS, for both steering wheels to leave DCS_Unknown.
'
' @returns bReady - TRUE when both did
'
' @local startMs - getms() when the wait began
' @local eLeftState - left wheel DCS_* sample
' @local eRightState - right wheel DCS_* sample

    bReady := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        beat(CP_LOOP_STEER_RDY)
        eLeftState, eRightState := steerStates()
        if (eLeftState <> steering.DCS_Unknown) and (eRightState <> steering.DCS_Unknown)
            bReady := TRUE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= READY_TIMEOUT_MS
            quit
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)

PRI bWaitSteerStopped() : bStopped | startMs
' Wait, bounded by STOP_TIMEOUT_MS, for both steering wheels to report STOPPED.
'
' @returns bStopped - TRUE when both did
'
' @local startMs - getms() when the wait began

    bStopped := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        beat(CP_LOOP_STEER_STOP)
        if isSteerStopped()
            bStopped := TRUE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= STOP_TIMEOUT_MS
            quit
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)

PRI steerStates() : eLeftState, eRightState
' Both steering wheels' driver state through the TEST-USE pass-through testGetDriverState().
'
' @returns eLeftState - left wheel DCS_*
' @returns eRightState - right wheel DCS_*

    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_READ)
    eLeftState, eRightState := steering.testGetDriverState()
    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_READ)

PRI steerTicks() : nLeftPos, nRightPos
' Both steering wheels' raw driver-maintained hall ticks through testGetRawHallTicks().
'
' @returns nLeftPos - left wheel raw hall ticks
' @returns nRightPos - right wheel raw hall ticks

    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_READ)
    nLeftPos, nRightPos := steering.testGetRawHallTicks()
    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_READ)

PRI isSteerStopped() : bStopped
' steering.isStopped(): TRUE when both wheels report STOPPED.
'
' @returns bStopped - TRUE when both are stopped

    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_READ)
    bStopped := steering.isStopped()
    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_READ)

PRI steerStopMotors()
' Command both steering wheels to stop through the public stopMotors().

    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_STOP)
    steering.stopMotors()
    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_STOP)

PRI steerStop()
' Stop the steering object: its sense cog, both driver cogs and both pin claims. Safe on a
' never-started or already-stopped instance. Cog 0 only: it beats. declareStall() calls
' steering.stop() directly instead.

    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_STOP)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    steering.stop()
    beat(CP_LIB_STEER_STOP)

PRI occupySpacers(maxSpacers) : startedCount | spawnedCog
' Start up to maxSpacers idle spacer cogs, stopping at the first cogspin() that returns < 0. The
' spacers never beat; this loop beats once per pass.
'
' @param maxSpacers - most spacers to start
' @returns startedCount - spacers now running, in spacerCog[0..startedCount-1]
'
' @local spawnedCog - cogspin()'s return (not newCog: names are case-insensitive, and NEWCOG is built in)

    startedCount := 0
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()                                ' the whole burst is one cog event (PL-85)
    repeat
        beat(CP_SPACER_LOOP)
        if (startedCount >= maxSpacers) or (startedCount >= SPACER_MAX)
            quit
        spawnedCog := cogspin(NEWCOG, spacerIdle(), @spacerStack[startedCount * SPACER_STACK_LONGS])
        if (spawnedCog < 0) or (spawnedCog > MAX_COG_ID)
            quit
        spacerCog[startedCount] := spawnedCog
        startedCount += 1
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()

PRI releaseSpacers(spacerCount) | spacerIdx
' Stop the first spacerCount spacer cogs.
'
' @param spacerCount - spacers to stop
'
' @local spacerIdx - index into spacerCog

    if spacerCount > 0                                      ' repeat 0 to -1 would count down, not skip
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()                            ' the whole burst is one cog event (PL-85)
        repeat spacerIdx from 0 to spacerCount - 1
            beat(CP_SPACER_LOOP)
            cogstop(spacerCog[spacerIdx])
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()

PRI spacerIdle()
' A spacer cog's whole life: idle until cogstop(). Runs in the spacer cog; never beats.

    repeat
        waitms(WD_IDLE_MS)

PRI runBrakeStartPhase() | brakeIdx, eLeftState, eRightState
' The brake-mode start phase (task 3521 phase D): R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART on this file's own wheels,
' per motor x sign, one BC-BRAKE each after that instance's wheel is stopped. The steering object
' is stop()ped first and must read DCS_Unknown on both wheels (PL-18); otherwise no instance runs
' and all four are NOMEAS.
'
' @local brakeIdx - BRK_* index
' @local eLeftState - steering left wheel DCS_* before the phase
' @local eRightState - steering right wheel DCS_* before the phase

    wdHoldIdx := WD_NO_HOLD
    wdSide := SIDE_NONE
    beat(CP_BRAKE)
    steerStop()
    eLeftState, eRightState := steerStates()
    bBrakeSteerClear := (eLeftState == steering.DCS_Unknown) and (eRightState == steering.DCS_Unknown)
    repeat brakeIdx from BRK_L_POS to BRAKE_COUNT - 1
        beat(CP_BRAKE)
        if bBrakeSteerClear
            measureBrakeStart(brakeIdx)
        emitBrake(brakeIdx)

PRI brakeInfo(brakeIdx) : side, sign
' Return which motor and increment sign one brake-start instance uses.
'
' @param brakeIdx - BRK_* index
' @returns side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns sign - +1 or -1

    case brakeIdx
        BRK_L_POS:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := 1
        BRK_L_NEG:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := -1
        BRK_R_POS:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := 1
        other:                                               ' BRK_R_NEG
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := -1

PRI measureBrakeStart(brakeIdx) | side, sign, startRet, ticksBefore, ticksAfter, eDrvrState, bDidFault
' Measure one brake-mode start into the brake VAR longs; prints nothing.
'
' SEQUENCE (task 3560, rebuilt on the front-cog contract): start(base, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
' -- the front cog releases the driver and owns every command from here -- then ready, then
' holdAtStop(TRUE) at rest and BRAKE_SETTLE_MS. The stopped driver compares stop_mode with the mode
' it last applied on every drive pass and, on the change, calls checkstop, which in SM_BRAKE runs
' initAngleFmHall and enables the drive: the same routine the old brake-mode start ran at driver
' start. This file never calls cogatn(): the harness must not strobe a driver a front cog owns (the
' old startEx(..., TRUE) + cogatn() sequence left this file's ATN latched once the front cog had
' released the driver itself). The cog id is used only when testGetMotorCog() agrees with it (P4
' positive control). Then ticks, signed PREFLIGHT_INCRE for PREFLIGHT_MS, ticks, zero, stopped,
' fault read, holdAtStop(FALSE), stop(). Motor frame: testDriveAtMotorIncrement() bypasses the
' reversed-motor flag, and forwardIsReverse() is never called on this file's wheels.
'
' WHAT THIS CELL CAN AND CANNOT PROVE (design sec A.5-h, corrected 2026-09-14): checkstop's
' "cmp stop_mode_, #SM_FLOAT wz / modz _nz wz / if_z call #initAngleFmHall" inverts the SM_FLOAT
' test, so initAngleFmHall -- which ends "mov prior_angle, angle_" -- runs only in SM_BRAKE. The
' uninitialised prior_angle that commit b34e109 fixed was the default SM_FLOAT start's, so this cell
' CANNOT fail on that defect. It is coverage of a drive commanded from a brake hold -- no fault,
' motion in the commanded direction.
'
' @param brakeIdx - BRK_* instance to measure
'
' @local side - SIDE_* of the instance
' @local sign - +1 or -1
' @local startRet - start()'s return
' @local ticksBefore - raw hall ticks before the window
' @local ticksAfter - raw hall ticks after the window
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* at the fault read
' @local bDidFault - fault latch at the fault read

    side, sign := brakeInfo(brakeIdx)
    wdHoldIdx := WD_NO_HOLD
    wdSide := side
    beat(CP_BRAKE)
    bBrakeRan[brakeIdx] := TRUE
    shutdownMotors()
    startRet := brakeStart(side)
    brakeStartRet[brakeIdx] := startRet
    if (startRet >= 0) and (startRet <= MAX_COG_ID)
        bBrakeStarted[brakeIdx] := (wheelMotorCog(side) == startRet + 1)
    if bBrakeStarted[brakeIdx]
        bBrakeReady[brakeIdx] := bWaitUntilReady(side)
        if bBrakeReady[brakeIdx]
            brakeHoldAtStop(side, TRUE)
            beat(CP_BRAKE_SETTLE)
            waitms(BRAKE_SETTLE_MS)
            beat(CP_BRAKE_SETTLE)
            ticksBefore := wheelTicks(side)
            commandMotor(side, sign * PREFLIGHT_INCRE)
            beat(CP_BRAKE_DRIVE)
            waitms(PREFLIGHT_MS)                            ' same increment magnitude and duration as the 13-tick measurement
            beat(CP_BRAKE_DRIVE)
            ticksAfter := wheelTicks(side)
            commandMotor(side, 0)
            bBrakeStopped[brakeIdx] := bWaitStoppedFor(side)
            brakeTicksDelta[brakeIdx] := ((ticksAfter - ticksBefore) #> (0 - LIM_SMALL)) <# LIM_SMALL
            if bWheelCogUp(side)
                ' the fault long is a latch (only clearFaultSignal() resets it), so this one read
                '  after the stop covers the whole window even though the zero command has
                '  already taken the driver out of DCS_FAULTED
                _, _, _, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
                bBrakeFault[brakeIdx] := bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
                bBrakeFaultRead[brakeIdx] := TRUE
        brakeHoldAtStop(side, FALSE)
    shutdownMotors()

PRI brakeStart(side) : startRet
' The named wheel's start(), bracketed by CP_LIB_BRAKE_START, for measureBrakeStart() and
' bClaimsFreeCheck(); start() returns a cog id 0..7 on success or -1 with the cause in getError().
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns startRet - start()'s return

    beat(CP_LIB_BRAKE_START)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startRet := wheelR.start(RIGHT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    else
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startRet := wheelL.start(LEFT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    beat(CP_LIB_BRAKE_START)

PRI brakeHoldAtStop(side, bEnable)
' holdAtStop() on the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @param bEnable - TRUE for SM_BRAKE, FALSE for SM_FLOAT

    beat(CP_LIB_HOLDATSTOP)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        wheelR.holdAtStop(bEnable)
    else
        wheelL.holdAtStop(bEnable)
    beat(CP_LIB_HOLDATSTOP)

PRI wheelMotorCog(side) : cogValue
' testGetMotorCog() of the named wheel: cog id + 1, or 0 when no driver cog runs.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns cogValue - the wheel's raw motorCog value

    beat(CP_LIB_COGUP)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        cogValue := wheelR.testGetMotorCog()
    else
        cogValue := wheelL.testGetMotorCog()
    beat(CP_LIB_COGUP)

PRI emitBanner()
' Emit BC-BANNER once. cfg_id is sourced from its own #ifdef, never a runtime test -- pnut-ts
' silently ignores an unknown -D, so a mistyped flag lands on the honest #else token. The pin
' bases, voltage and detect mode are stated outright so a log is attributable to hardware on its
' own evidence.
' Worst case: tag(9) + src_rev(16) + fmt(12) + cfg_id(13) + frame(12) + clkfreq(21) +
' left_base(15) + right_base(16) + voltage_enum(18) + det_mode(14) + hold_last(15) +
' qtr_incre(23) + half_incre(24) = 208 bytes.

    benchLog.begin(@"BC-BANNER")
    benchLog.numField(@"src_rev", SRC_REV, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"fmt", FMT_VERSION, LIM_SMALL)
#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    benchLog.tokenField(@"cfg_id", @sCfgBench, TOKMAX_CFG)
#else
    benchLog.tokenField(@"cfg_id", @sCfgUser, TOKMAX_CFG)
#endif
    benchLog.tokenField(@"frame", @sFrameMotor, TOKMAX_FRAME)
    benchLog.numField(@"clkfreq", CLKFREQ, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.numField(@"left_base", LEFT_TEST_BASE, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"right_base", RIGHT_TEST_BASE, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"voltage_enum", TEST_VOLTAGE, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"det_mode", TEST_DET_MODE, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"hold_last", HOLD_LAST, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"qtr_incre", QTR_SPEED_INCRE, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.numField(@"half_incre", HALF_SPEED_INCRE, LIM_BIG)
    lineEmit()

    beat(CP_NOTE)
    debug("* PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY -- emergencyCutoff() is a software stop, not a panic button")
    beat(CP_NOTE)

PRI emitPlan()
' Emit BC-PLAN once: every timing and wait bound the holds run under.
' Worst case: tag(7) + sample_ms(18) + zero_samples(21) + settle_ms(18) + window_ms(18) +
' ready_timeout_ms(25) + atspeed_timeout_ms(27) + steady_timeout_ms(26) + stop_timeout_ms(24) +
' hold0_motor(18) + steer_power(17) + steer_cmd_incre(29) = 248 bytes. steer_power and
' steer_cmd_incre are phase D's drive power and its commanded increment (STEER_CMD_INCRE: left +,
' right - after forwardIsReverse()).

    benchLog.begin(@"BC-PLAN")
    benchLog.numField(@"sample_ms", SAMPLE_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"zero_samples", ZERO_SAMPLES, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"settle_ms", SETTLE_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"window_ms", WINDOW_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"ready_timeout_ms", READY_TIMEOUT_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"atspeed_timeout_ms", ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"steady_timeout_ms", STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.numField(@"stop_timeout_ms", STOP_TIMEOUT_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"hold0_motor", motorToken(HOLD_ZERO_SIDE), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    benchLog.numField(@"steer_power", STEER_POWER, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"steer_cmd_incre", STEER_CMD_INCRE, LIM_BIG)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitWatchdogStart(bStarted, wdCog)
' Emit BC-WDSTART, the run's first record: whether the watchdog cog started, and its cog id.
' Worst case: tag(10) + started(14) + cog(9) = 33 bytes.
'
' @param bStarted - TRUE when cogspin() returned a cog id 0..MAX_COG_ID
' @param wdCog - cogspin()'s return for the watchdog

    benchLog.begin(@"BC-WDSTART")
    benchLog.boolField(@"started", bStarted)
    benchLog.numField(@"cog", wdCog, LIM_TINY)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitPreflight(side, startedCog, ticksMoved, bStopped)
' Emit BC-PREFLIGHT for one wheel. The base is chosen with if/else, and ok prints TRUE/FALSE.
' Worst case: tag(12) + motor(12) + base(10) + cog(9) + ticks(17) + ok(9) + stopped(14) = 83 bytes.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @param startedCog - start()'s return
' @param ticksMoved - signed tick delta across the nudge
' @param bStopped - TRUE when STOPPED was seen after the nudge

    benchLog.begin(@"BC-PREFLIGHT")
    benchLog.tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        benchLog.numField(@"base", RIGHT_TEST_BASE, LIM_TINY)
    else
        benchLog.numField(@"base", LEFT_TEST_BASE, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"cog", startedCog, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"ticks", ticksMoved, LIM_MID)
    benchLog.boolField(@"ok", (ticksMoved <> 0))
    benchLog.boolField(@"stopped", bStopped)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitHoldRecords(holdIdx)
' Emit one hold's records from its VAR longs, after its wheel has stopped: BC-SHEET, BC-START,
' BC-HOLD, BC-SENSE, BC-MOTION.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index

    emitSheet(holdIdx)
    emitStart(holdIdx)
    emitHold(holdIdx)
    emitSense(holdIdx)
    emitMotion(holdIdx)

PRI emitSheet(holdIdx) | pCaption
' Emit BC-SHEET: the hold's row number and caption (the caption names the frame).
' Worst case: tag(8) + row(9) + name(1+4+1+96=102) = 119 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local pCaption - pointer to the caption

    _, _, _, pCaption, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    benchLog.begin(@"BC-SHEET")
    benchLog.numField(@"row", holdIdx + 1, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"name", pCaption, TOKMAX_CAPTION)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitStart(holdIdx) | side, bStarted
' Emit BC-START: start() return, front cog id, detected board revision and drive constants
' (dead_gap in system ticks). Everything after cog prints NA when the driver did not start ready.
' Worst case: tag(8) + hold(10) + motor(12) + cog(9) + sense_cog(15) + board_rev(15) +
' board_id(17) + dead_gap(17) + pwm_limit(21) + duty_min(20) + duty_max(20) + adc_frame(21) +
' frame_cnt(21) = 206 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local side - SIDE_* of the hold
' @local bStarted - TRUE when the driver started and reported ready

    side, _, _, _, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    bStarted := bHoldStarted[holdIdx]
    benchLog.begin(@"BC-START")
    benchLog.numField(@"hold", holdIdx, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    benchLog.numField(@"cog", holdStartCog[holdIdx], LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"sense_cog", holdSenseCog[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bStarted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"board_rev", holdBoardRev[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bStarted)
    if bStarted
        benchLog.tokenField(@"board_id", boardToken(holdBoardRev[holdIdx]), TOKMAX_BOARD)
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"board_id", @sNa)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"dead_gap", holdDeadGap[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bStarted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"pwm_limit", holdPwmLimit[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"duty_min", holdDutyMin[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"duty_max", holdDutyMax[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"adc_frame", holdAdcFrame[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"frame_cnt", holdFrameCnt[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitHold(holdIdx) | side, pRobotTok, pRungTok
' Emit BC-HOLD: identity (signed increment, robot_dir, frame), result and wait outcomes.
' Worst case: tag(7) + hold(10) + motor(12) + incre(19) + robot_dir(15) + frame(12) + rung(10) +
' result(22) + at_speed(15) + steady_ms(18) + steady_src(19) + steady_rate(20) + stopped(14) =
' 193 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local side - SIDE_* of the hold
' @local pRobotTok - robot-frame direction token
' @local pRungTok - speed-rung token

    side, _, _, _, pRobotTok, pRungTok := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    benchLog.begin(@"BC-HOLD")
    benchLog.numField(@"hold", holdIdx, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    benchLog.numField(@"incre", holdIncre[holdIdx], LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"robot_dir", pRobotTok, TOKMAX_ROBOT)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"frame", @sFrameMotor, TOKMAX_FRAME)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"rung", pRungTok, TOKMAX_RUNG)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"result", resultToken(holdResultCode[holdIdx]), TOKMAX_RESULT)
    if holdIncre[holdIdx] <> 0
        benchLog.boolField(@"at_speed", bHoldAtSpeed[holdIdx])
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"at_speed", @sNa)                    ' hold 0 never commands motion
    benchLog.naNumField(@"steady_ms", holdSteadyMs[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bHoldStarted[holdIdx] and (holdIncre[holdIdx] <> 0))
    if holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] <> 0
        benchLog.tokenField(@"steady_src", holdSteadySrc[holdIdx], TOKMAX_STEADY)
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"steady_src", @sNa)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"steady_rate", holdSteadyRate[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] <> 0)
    benchLog.boolField(@"stopped", bHoldStopped[holdIdx])
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSense(holdIdx) | bWindow, bZero, bBoardKnown
' Emit BC-SENSE: the window's raw sense mean, the same-lifetime zero, their difference (net), and
' getCurrent()'s window mean. Amps print NA unless the board was detected as REV_A or REV_B:
' isp_bldc_motor.spin2 init() leaves rSenseForBoard at -1 otherwise, and getCurrent() then divides by
' it (PL-25). The window min/max and watts it once printed fed no cell and no finding (task 3574).
' Worst case: tag(8) + hold(10) + samples(16) + win_ms(15) + zero_samples(21) + raw_mV_x10(24) +
' zero_mV_x10(25) + net_mV_x10(24) + amps_x10k(21) = 164 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local bWindow - TRUE when the window took at least one sample
' @local bZero - TRUE when the zero took at least one sample
' @local bBoardKnown - TRUE when the start-time board revision is REV_A or REV_B

    bWindow := (holdSamples[holdIdx] > 0)
    bZero := (holdZeroSamples[holdIdx] > 0)
    bBoardKnown := (holdBoardRev[holdIdx] == wheelL.REV_A) or (holdBoardRev[holdIdx] == wheelL.REV_B)
    benchLog.begin(@"BC-SENSE")
    benchLog.numField(@"hold", holdIdx, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.numField(@"samples", holdSamples[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"win_ms", holdWinMs[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bWindow)
    benchLog.numField(@"zero_samples", holdZeroSamples[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"raw_mV_x10", holdRawX10[holdIdx], LIM_BIG, bWindow)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"zero_mV_x10", holdZeroX10[holdIdx], LIM_BIG, bZero)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"net_mV_x10", holdNetX10[holdIdx], LIM_BIG, bWindow and bZero)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"amps_x10k", holdAmpsMean[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bWindow and bBoardKnown)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitMotion(holdIdx) | bMotion, bWindow
' Emit BC-MOTION: rpm, ticks and tick rate over the window, applied offsets, duty and err window
' means, hall integrity counts since this hold's start, and the driver state after the stop wait.
' Worst case: tag(9) + hold(10) + rpm(12) + ticks(17) + rate_x10(17) + neg_deg(13) + pos_deg(13) +
' duty_mean(21) + err_mean(20) + missed(18) + illegal(19) + drv_state(15) = 184 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local bMotion - TRUE when the window ran and the cog was up at its end
' @local bWindow - TRUE when the window took at least one sample

    bMotion := bHoldMotionValid[holdIdx]
    bWindow := (holdSamples[holdIdx] > 0)
    benchLog.begin(@"BC-MOTION")
    benchLog.numField(@"hold", holdIdx, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"rpm", holdRpm[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bMotion and (holdSenseCog[holdIdx] >= 0))
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ticks", holdTicks[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bMotion)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"rate_x10", holdRateX10[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bMotion)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"neg_deg", holdNegDeg[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bMotion)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"pos_deg", holdPosDeg[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bMotion)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"duty_mean", holdDutyMean[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bWindow)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"err_mean", holdErrMean[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bWindow)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"missed", holdMissed[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx])
    benchLog.naNumField(@"illegal", holdIllegal[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx])
    benchLog.naNumField(@"drv_state", holdDrvState[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx])
    lineEmit()

PRI emitEnd(trapCode)
' Emit BC-END, the last record before the end marker. P3 (task 3539): trap is printed on EVERY
' run, not only when lib_abort is TRUE -- a free check that the single top-level trap's value is
' 0 (its normal, no-abort return) whenever the run completed.
' Worst case: tag(6) + exit(14) + preflight_ok(19) + holds_run(15) + lib_abort(16) + trap(16) =
' 86 bytes.
'
' @param trapCode - value the top-level trap around \bRunSession() delivered, printed unconditionally

    benchLog.begin(@"BC-END")
    if bRunReturned and bPreflightOk and (holdsRun == HOLD_LAST + 1)
        benchLog.tokenField(@"exit", @sExitComplete, TOKMAX_EXIT)
    else
        benchLog.tokenField(@"exit", @sExitAborted, TOKMAX_EXIT)
    benchLog.boolField(@"preflight_ok", bPreflightOk)
    benchLog.numField(@"holds_run", holdsRun, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.boolField(@"lib_abort", (bRunReturned == FALSE))
    benchLog.numField(@"trap", trapCode, LIM_MID)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSignoffDecls()
' Emit one SIGNOFF-DECL per cell this binary judges, right after BC-PLAN (task 3521 phase C).
'

    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellSense, @sSfTaskSense)
    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellRpm, @sSfTaskRpm)
    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellIscale, @sSfTaskIscale)
    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellInteg, @sSfTaskInteg)
    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellSteerFail, @sSfTaskSteer)       ' task 3521 phase D
    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellSteerStart, @sSfTaskSteer)
    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellSteerLive, @sSfTaskSteer)
    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellBrake, @sSfTaskBrake)
    emitSignoffDecl(@sSfCellSteerErr, @sSfTaskErr)          ' task 3560

PRI emitSignoffDecl(pCell, pTask)
' Emit SIGNOFF-DECL for one cell.
' Worst case, by clamp widths: tag(12) + sf(8) + bin(11) + cell(26) + task(11) = 68 bytes.
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id token
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task id, as plain text

    benchLog.begin(@"SIGNOFF-DECL")
    benchLog.numField(@"sf", SF_VERSION, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"bin", @sSfBinChar, TOKMAX_BIN)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"cell", pCell, TOKMAX_CELL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"task", pTask, TOKMAX_TASK)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSignoffs() | holdIdx, side, bMeasured, measuredVal, instCount
' Emit every declared cell's SIGNOFF instances from the per-hold results: R5, R4 and R2 once per
' motion hold (holds 1..8, all eight whether or not they ran -- a hold never reached is NOT_RUN and
' gives NOMEAS), then R3 once per motor, then the phase D cells (emitPhaseDSignoffs()). Runs on
' cog 0's normal end path only, after every wheel is stopped; no library call, no wait.
'
' @local holdIdx - HOLD_* motion hold
' @local side - SIDE_* of the hold, or the motor of an R3 instance
' @local bMeasured - TRUE when the instance was measured
' @local measuredVal - the instance's measured value
' @local instCount - samples, ticks or holds behind measuredVal

    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_L_FWD_QTR to HOLD_R_REV_HALF
        beat(CP_EMIT)
        side, _, _, _, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
        bMeasured, measuredVal, instCount := senseSignoffValue(holdIdx)
        emitSignoff(@sSfCellSense, @sSfTaskSense, side, @sSfCritSense, bMeasured, measuredVal, SENSE_PCT_X10_LO, SENSE_PCT_X10_HI, @sSfUnitsPct, instCount)
    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_L_FWD_QTR to HOLD_R_REV_HALF
        beat(CP_EMIT)
        side, _, _, _, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
        bMeasured, measuredVal, instCount := rpmSignoffValue(holdIdx)
        emitSignoff(@sSfCellRpm, @sSfTaskRpm, side, @sSfCritRpm, bMeasured, measuredVal, RPM_ERR_LO, RPM_ERR_HI, @sSfUnitsRpm, instCount)
    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_L_FWD_QTR to HOLD_R_REV_HALF
        beat(CP_EMIT)
        side, _, _, _, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
        bMeasured, measuredVal, instCount := iscaleSignoffValue(holdIdx)
        emitSignoff(@sSfCellIscale, @sSfTaskIscale, side, @sSfCritIscale, bMeasured, measuredVal, RSENSE_IMPLIED_LO, RSENSE_IMPLIED_HI, @sSfUnitsCount, instCount)
    repeat side from SIDE_LEFT to SIDE_RIGHT
        beat(CP_EMIT)
        bMeasured, measuredVal, instCount := integSignoffValue(side)
        emitSignoff(@sSfCellInteg, @sSfTaskInteg, side, @sSfCritInteg, bMeasured, measuredVal, INTEG_SUM_LO, INTEG_SUM_HI, @sSfUnitsCount, instCount)
    emitPhaseDSignoffs()

PRI isWindowTrusted(holdIdx) : bTrusted
' Report whether a hold's measurement window can feed a cell: the hold ran to RES_OK and, for a motion hold,
' reached steadiness by its own rate check rather than by timing out (task 3574). A TIMEOUT window may still
' hold the end of the ramp, so it is printed but judged NOMEAS rather than passed.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @returns bTrusted - TRUE when the window can be judged

    bTrusted := (holdResultCode[holdIdx] == RES_OK) and (holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] <> @sSteadyTimeout)

PRI senseSignoffValue(holdIdx) : bMeasured, measuredVal, sampleCount | milliAmps, expectedX10, diffX10
' R5-CHAR-SENSE for one motion hold: the net sense mean against Pass 1's expected net, percent x10.
'   expectedX10 = PASS1_FIT_MV_X10_PER_A x A_mA / 1000   (<= 1501 x 5_564 = 8_351_564 before the
'                 divide; every operand positive, so the divide truncates down: at most 0.1 mV low)
'   measuredVal = (holdNetX10 - expectedX10) x 1000 / expectedX10
' holdNetX10 is within +/-2e9 (sampleWindow() clamps both operands to LIM_BIG), so the subtraction
' of at most 8_351 stays above NEGX; the difference is then clamped to +/-SENSE_DIFF_X10_LIMIT, so x
' 1000 is within +/-2e9 < POSX. The smallest divisor is 804 (hold 1), never 0. The final divide is
' signed; for a negative difference its rounding direction (toward zero or down) is UNVERIFIED
' here, and moves the result by less than 1 unit (0.1 %) either way. NOMEAS when the hold's window is not
' trusted (isWindowTrusted()), its window or its zero took no samples, or it has no Pass 1 value.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* motion hold
' @returns bMeasured - TRUE when the instance was measured
' @returns measuredVal - percent x10 deviation from the Pass 1 expectation, 0 when not measured
' @returns sampleCount - window samples behind the mean, 0 when not measured
'
' @local milliAmps - Pass 1 meter current for this hold, mA
' @local expectedX10 - expected net sense, mV x10
' @local diffX10 - net minus expected, clamped, mV x10

    bMeasured := FALSE
    measuredVal := 0
    sampleCount := 0
    milliAmps := LONG[@pass1HoldMilliAmps][holdIdx]
    if isWindowTrusted(holdIdx) and (holdSamples[holdIdx] > 0) and (holdZeroSamples[holdIdx] > 0) and (milliAmps > 0)
        expectedX10 := (PASS1_FIT_MV_X10_PER_A * milliAmps) / MA_PER_A
        if expectedX10 > 0
            diffX10 := ((holdNetX10[holdIdx] - expectedX10) #> (0 - SENSE_DIFF_X10_LIMIT)) <# SENSE_DIFF_X10_LIMIT
            measuredVal := (diffX10 * PCT_X10_PER_UNIT) / expectedX10
            sampleCount := holdSamples[holdIdx]
            bMeasured := TRUE

PRI rpmSignoffValue(holdIdx) : bMeasured, measuredVal, tickCount | expectedRpm, rpmMagnitude
' R4-CHAR-RPM for one motion hold: the library's rpm against the rpm this file's own tick rate
' implies. testGetRpm() returns rpm = (hallWindowSum x 60 x 10 / 90) / 10, and hallWindowSum is a
' sum of absDistanceInTics() = abs() deltas (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 updateWindowAccumulators(),
' updateHdmiData()), so rpm is a non-negative magnitude for either increment sign; abs() is taken
' anyway. holdRateX10 is non-negative (abs ticks) and at most 999_990_000, so + 7 cannot overflow:
'   expectedRpm = (holdRateX10 + RPM_ROUND_HALF_X10) / RATE_X10_PER_RPM   (round to nearest)
'   measuredVal = |holdRpm| - expectedRpm, both operands within 0..LIM_BIG
' NOMEAS when the window is not trusted (isWindowTrusted()), the motion fields are not valid, the front
' cog did not start, or nothing moved by either measure (ticks 0 and rpm 0: agreement at zero proves nothing).
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* motion hold
' @returns bMeasured - TRUE when the instance was measured
' @returns measuredVal - rpm error, 0 when not measured
' @returns tickCount - hall ticks over the window behind the tick rate, 0 when not measured
'
' @local expectedRpm - rpm implied by the window's tick rate, rounded to nearest
' @local rpmMagnitude - |testGetRpm()| clamped to LIM_BIG

    bMeasured := FALSE
    measuredVal := 0
    tickCount := 0
    if isWindowTrusted(holdIdx) and (bHoldMotionValid[holdIdx] == TRUE) and (holdSenseCog[holdIdx] >= 0)
        rpmMagnitude := absValue((holdRpm[holdIdx] #> (0 - LIM_BIG)) <# LIM_BIG)
        if (holdTicks[holdIdx] <> 0) or (rpmMagnitude <> 0)
            expectedRpm := ((holdRateX10[holdIdx] #> 0) + RPM_ROUND_HALF_X10) / RATE_X10_PER_RPM
            measuredVal := rpmMagnitude - expectedRpm
            tickCount := holdTicks[holdIdx]
            bMeasured := TRUE

PRI iscaleSignoffValue(holdIdx) : bMeasured, measuredVal, sampleCount | rawX10, ampsMean, ampsPerThousand, quotVal, bBoardKnown
' R2-CHAR-ISCALE for one motion hold: the sense resistance getCurrent() used, recovered from its
' two window means. Units: holdRawX10 is mV x10 and holdAmpsMean is amps x 10_000, so
'   measuredVal = holdRawX10 x 1000 / holdAmpsMean = (10 mV)(1000) / (10_000 A) = mV / A
' which is rSenseForBoard: 150 on Rev B, 5 on a board detected as Rev A. At the largest plausible
' raw mean (half speed ~900 mV, holdRawX10 9_000) the product is 9_000_000, far under POSX; the
' direct form is used up to ISCALE_DIRECT_RAW_X10_MAX (product 2e9). Beyond it (a scale regression
' only) the divide goes first, so nothing overflows: by holdAmpsMean / 1000 when that is at least
' 1 (within 0.01 % wherever the ratio is near the band), otherwise the quotient clamped to
' ISCALE_QUOT_MAX then x 1000 (there the ratio exceeds 2_000_000, far outside the band). NOMEAS when
' the window is not trusted (isWindowTrusted()), the window took no samples, the start-time board revision is not REV_A
' or REV_B (PL-25: getCurrent() divides by -1 then), or holdAmpsMean <= 0.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* motion hold
' @returns bMeasured - TRUE when the instance was measured
' @returns measuredVal - implied sense resistance in mV per amp, 0 when not measured
' @returns sampleCount - window samples behind the means, 0 when not measured
'
' @local rawX10 - window raw sense mean, mV x10
' @local ampsMean - window getCurrent() mean, amps x 10_000
' @local ampsPerThousand - ampsMean / ISCALE_RATIO_SCALE, for the divide-first form
' @local quotVal - rawX10 / ampsMean, clamped, for the divide-first form
' @local bBoardKnown - TRUE when the start-time board revision is REV_A or REV_B

    bMeasured := FALSE
    measuredVal := 0
    sampleCount := 0
    bBoardKnown := (holdBoardRev[holdIdx] == wheelL.REV_A) or (holdBoardRev[holdIdx] == wheelL.REV_B)
    ampsMean := holdAmpsMean[holdIdx]
    if isWindowTrusted(holdIdx) and (holdSamples[holdIdx] > 0) and bBoardKnown and (ampsMean > 0)
        rawX10 := holdRawX10[holdIdx]
        if absValue(rawX10) <= ISCALE_DIRECT_RAW_X10_MAX
            measuredVal := (rawX10 * ISCALE_RATIO_SCALE) / ampsMean
        else
            ampsPerThousand := ampsMean / ISCALE_RATIO_SCALE
            if ampsPerThousand > 0
                measuredVal := rawX10 / ampsPerThousand
            else
                quotVal := ((rawX10 / ampsMean) #> (0 - ISCALE_QUOT_MAX)) <# ISCALE_QUOT_MAX
                measuredVal := quotVal * ISCALE_RATIO_SCALE
        sampleCount := holdSamples[holdIdx]
        bMeasured := TRUE

PRI integSignoffValue(side) : bMeasured, integSum, holdCount | holdIdx, holdSide
' R3-CHAR-INTEG for one motor: missed + illegal hall counts summed over every hold of that motor
' whose counts were read from a running cog, including hold 0 for HOLD_ZERO_SIDE. Each count's
' magnitude is clamped to LIM_MID, so a negative (corrupt) count still adds and the sum is at most
' 9 x 2 x 9_999_999 < POSX. NOMEAS with n 0 when no hold of that motor has valid counts.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bMeasured - TRUE when at least one hold's counts were summed
' @returns integSum - missed + illegal over the summed holds
' @returns holdCount - holds summed
'
' @local holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @local holdSide - SIDE_* of that hold

    integSum := 0
    holdCount := 0
    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_ZERO to HOLD_COUNT - 1
        beat(CP_EMIT)
        holdSide, _, _, _, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
        if (holdSide == side) and (bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx] == TRUE)
            integSum += (absValue(holdMissed[holdIdx]) <# LIM_MID) + (absValue(holdIllegal[holdIdx]) <# LIM_MID)
            holdCount += 1
    bMeasured := (holdCount > 0)

PRI emitSignoff(pCell, pTask, side, pCrit, bMeasured, measuredVal, loLimit, hiLimit, pUnits, instCount) | boundedVal, pVerdict
' Emit one SIGNOFF verdict (design sec B.1, sf 1) from the existing line builder. measured is
' clamped to LIM_BIG first and the verdict is judged on that printed value, so a record always
' agrees with its own numbers (every limit here is far inside LIM_BIG). PASS only when measured
' AND in loLimit..hiLimit; FAIL when measured and outside; NOMEAS, with measured NA and n 0, when
' not measured.
' Worst case, by clamp widths: tag(7) + sf(8) + bin(11) + cell(26) + task(11) + motor(12) +
' crit(24) + measured(22) + lo(16) + hi(16) + units(15) + n(10) + verdict(18) = 196 bytes.
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id token
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task id, as plain text
' @param side - SIDE_* the instance belongs to
' @param pCrit - pointer to the criterion token
' @param bMeasured - TRUE when the instance was measured
' @param measuredVal - the instance's measured value
' @param loLimit - lowest passing value, compiled in
' @param hiLimit - highest passing value, compiled in
' @param pUnits - pointer to the units token
' @param instCount - samples, ticks or holds behind measuredVal
'
' @local boundedVal - measuredVal clamped to +/-LIM_BIG
' @local pVerdict - PASS, FAIL or NOMEAS token

    boundedVal := (measuredVal #> (0 - LIM_BIG)) <# LIM_BIG
    if bMeasured == FALSE
        pVerdict := @sSfNomeas
    elseif (boundedVal >= loLimit) and (boundedVal <= hiLimit)
        pVerdict := @sSfPass
    else
        pVerdict := @sSfFail
    benchLog.begin(@"SIGNOFF")
    benchLog.numField(@"sf", SF_VERSION, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"bin", @sSfBinChar, TOKMAX_BIN)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"cell", pCell, TOKMAX_CELL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"task", pTask, TOKMAX_TASK)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"crit", pCrit, TOKMAX_CRIT)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"measured", boundedVal, LIM_BIG, bMeasured)
    benchLog.numField(@"lo", loLimit, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.numField(@"hi", hiLimit, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"units", pUnits, TOKMAX_UNITS)
    if bMeasured
        benchLog.numField(@"n", instCount, LIM_SMALL)
    else
        benchLog.numField(@"n", 0, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"verdict", pVerdict, TOKMAX_SFVERDICT)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitPhaseDSignoffs() | side, sign, brakeIdx, measuredVal, bCriterionMet
' Emit the phase D verdicts (task 3521 phase D) from the phase VAR longs: R10-CHAR-STEERFAIL,
' R10-CHAR-STEERSTART, R10-CHAR-STEERLIVE per wheel, R13-CHAR-BRAKESTART per motor x sign. An
' instance never reached keeps initPhaseD()'s not-run state and prints NOMEAS with n 0.
'  STEERFAIL  measured = TRUE/FALSE, units BOOL: TRUE when start() returned -1 AND free-after ==
'             baseline AND bClaimsFreeCheck() passed (PL-36) AND no abort; the numbers are in
'             BC-STEER. NOMEAS when the baseline was below STEERFAIL_MIN_BASELINE, or the spacers did
'             not leave exactly one cog free.
'  STEERERR   measured = TRUE/FALSE, units BOOL, motor RIGHT (task 3560): TRUE when the failed start's
'             getError() gave the right wheel ERR_NO_FREE_COG and the left wheel NO_ERROR; the three
'             codes are in BC-STEERERR. NOMEAS exactly when STEERFAIL is.
'  STEERSTART measured = TRUE/FALSE, units BOOL: TRUE when start() returned 0..7 AND both wheels
'             left DCS_Unknown AND no abort; the numbers are in BC-STEER. NOMEAS when not reached.
'  STEERLIVE  measured = |raw tick delta| per wheel, lo 6 hi NA. NOMEAS when start() returned
'             outside 0..7 or aborted.
'  BRAKESTART measured = TRUE/FALSE, units BOOL: TRUE when the fault state was read from a
'             running driver AND no fault AND sign x delta >= LIVENESS_MIN_TICKS (the tick sign
'             equals the increment sign and |delta| >= 6). The numbers are in that instance's
'             BC-BRAKE. NOMEAS when start() failed, or the driver never became ready. Every
'             library call in this phase (task 3539) is called UNTRAPPED; a genuine abort is
'             caught by main()'s single top-level trap instead, which ends the whole run before
'             any of these cells is even reached.
' Every multi-condition criterion is a BOOL verdict, so each record agrees with its own measured
' field (arbiter review 2026-09-14).
'
' @local side - SIDE_* of the instance
' @local sign - +1 or -1 for a brake-start instance
' @local brakeIdx - BRK_* index
' @local measuredVal - the steering-live instance's tick delta
' @local bCriterionMet - the brake-start instance's boolean result

    beat(CP_EMIT)
    emitSignoffBool(@sSfCellSteerFail, @sSfTaskSteer, SIDE_NONE, @sSfCritNoLeak, bSteerFailMeasured, (steerFailReturn == STEERFAIL_RET) and (steerFailFreeAfter == steerFailBaseline) and (bSteerFailClaimsFree == TRUE), SIGNOFF_ONE_INSTANCE)
    beat(CP_EMIT)
    emitSignoffBool(@sSfCellSteerErr, @sSfTaskErr, SIDE_RIGHT, @sSfCritWheel, bSteerFailMeasured, (steerFailRtError == STEERERR_FAILED_WHEEL_CODE) and (steerFailLtError == STEERERR_OK_CODE), SIGNOFF_ONE_INSTANCE)
    beat(CP_EMIT)
    emitSignoffBool(@sSfCellSteerStart, @sSfTaskSteer, SIDE_NONE, @sSfCritStartCog, bSteerStartRan, (steerStartReturn >= STEERSTART_COG_LO) and (steerStartReturn <= STEERSTART_COG_HI) and (bSteerBothReady == TRUE), SIGNOFF_ONE_INSTANCE)
    repeat side from SIDE_LEFT to SIDE_RIGHT
        beat(CP_EMIT)
        measuredVal := (side == SIDE_RIGHT) ? steerRtTicksDelta : steerLtTicksDelta     ' selects values only (PL-29)
        emitSignoffEx(@sSfCellSteerLive, @sSfTaskSteer, side, @sSfCritTicks, bSteerLiveRan, measuredVal, LIVENESS_MIN_TICKS, TRUE, 0, FALSE, TRUE, @sSfUnitsTicks, SIGNOFF_ONE_INSTANCE)
    repeat brakeIdx from BRK_L_POS to BRAKE_COUNT - 1
        beat(CP_EMIT)
        side, sign := brakeInfo(brakeIdx)
        ' brakeTicksDelta is clamped to +/-LIM_SMALL, so sign x delta cannot overflow
        bCriterionMet := (bBrakeFaultRead[brakeIdx] == TRUE) and (bBrakeFault[brakeIdx] == FALSE) and ((sign * brakeTicksDelta[brakeIdx]) >= LIVENESS_MIN_TICKS)
        emitSignoffBool(@sSfCellBrake, @sSfTaskBrake, side, @sSfCritBrake, bBrakeStarted[brakeIdx] and bBrakeReady[brakeIdx], bCriterionMet, SIGNOFF_ONE_INSTANCE)

PRI emitSignoffEx(pCell, pTask, side, pCrit, bMeasured, measuredVal, loLimit, bHasLo, hiLimit, bHasHi, bConditionsOk, pUnits, instCount) | boundedVal, pVerdict
' Emit one SIGNOFF verdict (design sec B.1, sf 1) whose limits may be NA and whose PASS may need a
' condition beyond lo..hi. Same fields, order and clamps as emitSignoff(), which can do neither.
' PASS only when measured AND bConditionsOk AND every present limit holds; FAIL when measured
' otherwise; NOMEAS, with measured NA and n 0, when not measured. Judged on the clamped value.
' Worst case, by clamp widths: identical to emitSignoff(), 196 bytes (an NA limit is shorter).
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id token
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task id, as plain text
' @param side - SIDE_* the instance belongs to
' @param pCrit - pointer to the criterion token
' @param bMeasured - TRUE when the instance was measured
' @param measuredVal - the instance's measured value
' @param loLimit - lowest passing value, compiled in (ignored when bHasLo is FALSE)
' @param bHasLo - TRUE when the cell has a low limit; FALSE prints lo NA
' @param hiLimit - highest passing value, compiled in (ignored when bHasHi is FALSE)
' @param bHasHi - TRUE when the cell has a high limit; FALSE prints hi NA
' @param bConditionsOk - TRUE when every non-range condition of the criterion holds
' @param pUnits - pointer to the units token
' @param instCount - samples, ticks or starts behind measuredVal
'
' @local boundedVal - measuredVal clamped to +/-LIM_BIG
' @local pVerdict - PASS, FAIL or NOMEAS token

    boundedVal := (measuredVal #> (0 - LIM_BIG)) <# LIM_BIG
    if bMeasured == FALSE
        pVerdict := @sSfNomeas
    elseif (bConditionsOk == TRUE) and ((bHasLo == FALSE) or (boundedVal >= loLimit)) and ((bHasHi == FALSE) or (boundedVal <= hiLimit))
        pVerdict := @sSfPass
    else
        pVerdict := @sSfFail
    benchLog.begin(@"SIGNOFF")
    benchLog.numField(@"sf", SF_VERSION, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"bin", @sSfBinChar, TOKMAX_BIN)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"cell", pCell, TOKMAX_CELL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"task", pTask, TOKMAX_TASK)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"crit", pCrit, TOKMAX_CRIT)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"measured", boundedVal, LIM_BIG, bMeasured)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"lo", loLimit, LIM_BIG, bHasLo)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"hi", hiLimit, LIM_BIG, bHasHi)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"units", pUnits, TOKMAX_UNITS)
    if bMeasured
        benchLog.numField(@"n", instCount, LIM_SMALL)
    else
        benchLog.numField(@"n", 0, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"verdict", pVerdict, TOKMAX_SFVERDICT)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSignoffBool(pCell, pTask, side, pCrit, bMeasured, bCriterionMet, instCount) | pVerdict
' Emit one boolean SIGNOFF verdict (design sec B.1, sf 1): measured TRUE/FALSE (NA when not
' measured), lo TRUE, hi TRUE, units BOOL. PASS only when measured AND TRUE, so the verdict always
' agrees with its own measured field.
' Worst case: tag(7) + sf(8) + bin(11) + cell(26) + task(11) + motor(12) + crit(24) + measured(15)
' + lo(8) + hi(8) + units(15) + n(10) + verdict(18) = 173 bytes.
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id token
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task id, as plain text
' @param side - SIDE_* the instance belongs to
' @param pCrit - pointer to the criterion token
' @param bMeasured - TRUE when the instance was measured
' @param bCriterionMet - TRUE when the whole criterion held
' @param instCount - starts or windows behind the result

' Local Variables:
' @local pVerdict - PASS, FAIL or NOMEAS token

    if bMeasured == FALSE
        pVerdict := @sSfNomeas
    elseif bCriterionMet == TRUE
        pVerdict := @sSfPass
    else
        pVerdict := @sSfFail
    benchLog.begin(@"SIGNOFF")
    benchLog.numField(@"sf", SF_VERSION, LIM_TINY)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"bin", @sSfBinChar, TOKMAX_BIN)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"cell", pCell, TOKMAX_CELL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"task", pTask, TOKMAX_TASK)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"crit", pCrit, TOKMAX_CRIT)
    if bMeasured
        benchLog.boolField(@"measured", bCriterionMet)
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"measured", @sNa)
    benchLog.textField(@"lo", @sTrue)
    benchLog.textField(@"hi", @sTrue)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"units", @sSfUnitsBool, TOKMAX_UNITS)
    if bMeasured
        benchLog.numField(@"n", instCount, LIM_SMALL)
    else
        benchLog.numField(@"n", 0, LIM_SMALL)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"verdict", pVerdict, TOKMAX_SFVERDICT)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSteer() | bMovedBoth
' Emit BC-STEER once, after steering.stop(): the STEERFAIL cog arithmetic and PL-36 claim check,
' the normal start, the wheels' driver-state evidence and each wheel's tick delta. The drive power
' and its commanded increment are compile-time constants, printed once in BC-PLAN. A field whose
' step did not run prints NA. Task 3539 (P5): drive_done reports driveAtPower()'s own returned
' value directly -- it is no longer folded into an "aborted" flag that conflated a wrong value
' with a real abort; every call in this phase is UNTRAPPED, and a genuine abort is caught by
' main()'s single top-level trap instead.
' Worst case: tag(8) + steer_fail_return(23) + fail_baseline(19) + fail_spacers(18) +
' fail_free_after(21) + claims_free(18) + start_return(18) + drive_done(16) + l_state(13) +
' r_state(13) + both_ready(17) + l_ticks_delta(22) + r_ticks_delta(22) + moved_both(17) +
' stopped(14) = 259 bytes.
'
' @local bMovedBoth - TRUE when both wheels' deltas reached LIVENESS_MIN_TICKS

    bMovedBoth := bSteerLiveRan and (steerLtTicksDelta >= LIVENESS_MIN_TICKS) and (steerRtTicksDelta >= LIVENESS_MIN_TICKS)
    benchLog.begin(@"BC-STEER")
    benchLog.naNumField(@"steer_fail_return", steerFailReturn, LIM_TINY, bSteerFailAttempted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"fail_baseline", steerFailBaseline, LIM_TINY, bSteerFailCounted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"fail_spacers", steerFailSpacers, LIM_TINY, bSteerFailAttempted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"fail_free_after", steerFailFreeAfter, LIM_TINY, bSteerFailAttempted)
    if bSteerFailAttempted
        benchLog.boolField(@"claims_free", bSteerFailClaimsFree)
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"claims_free", @sNa)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"start_return", steerStartReturn, LIM_TINY, bSteerStartRan)
    if bSteerBothReady
        benchLog.boolField(@"drive_done", bSteerDriveDone)
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"drive_done", @sNa)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"l_state", steerLtState, LIM_TINY, bSteerLiveRan)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"r_state", steerRtState, LIM_TINY, bSteerLiveRan)
    benchLog.boolField(@"both_ready", bSteerBothReady)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"l_ticks_delta", steerLtTicksDelta, LIM_SMALL, bSteerLiveRan)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"r_ticks_delta", steerRtTicksDelta, LIM_SMALL, bSteerLiveRan)
    benchLog.boolField(@"moved_both", bMovedBoth)
    benchLog.boolField(@"stopped", bSteerStopped)
    lineEmit()
    emitSteerErr()

PRI emitSteerErr()
' Emit BC-STEERERR once, right after BC-STEER (task 3560): steering.getError()'s three results read
' just after the STEERFAIL start. Each prints NA when that start was not attempted.
' Worst case: tag(11) + error(17) + l_error(19) + r_error(19) = 66 bytes.

    benchLog.begin(@"BC-STEERERR")
    benchLog.naNumField(@"error", steerFailError, LIM_SMALL, bSteerFailAttempted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"l_error", steerFailLtError, LIM_SMALL, bSteerFailAttempted)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"r_error", steerFailRtError, LIM_SMALL, bSteerFailAttempted)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitBrake(brakeIdx) | side, sign, bRan
' Emit BC-BRAKE for one brake-start instance, after its wheel is stopped: motor, signed motor
' increment, frame, whether it ran, start()'s return, ready, signed tick delta, fault,
' stopped. A field whose step did not run prints NA. start() is called UNTRAPPED, so
' there is no longer a per-instance abort flag to report -- a genuine abort is caught by main()'s
' single top-level trap.
' Worst case: tag(8) + motor(12) + incre(19) + frame(12) + ran(10) + start_return(18) +
' ready(12) + ticks_delta(20) + fault(12) + stopped(14) = 137 bytes.
'
' @param brakeIdx - BRK_* index
'
' @local side - SIDE_* of the instance
' @local sign - +1 or -1
' @local bRan - TRUE when the instance was reached

    side, sign := brakeInfo(brakeIdx)
    bRan := bBrakeRan[brakeIdx]
    benchLog.begin(@"BC-BRAKE")
    benchLog.tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    benchLog.numField(@"incre", sign * PREFLIGHT_INCRE, LIM_BIG)
    benchLog.tokenField(@"frame", @sFrameMotor, TOKMAX_FRAME)
    benchLog.boolField(@"ran", bRan)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"start_return", brakeStartRet[brakeIdx], LIM_TINY, bRan)
    if bBrakeStarted[brakeIdx]
        benchLog.boolField(@"ready", bBrakeReady[brakeIdx])
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"ready", @sNa)
    benchLog.naNumField(@"ticks_delta", brakeTicksDelta[brakeIdx], LIM_SMALL, bBrakeReady[brakeIdx])
    if bBrakeFaultRead[brakeIdx]
        benchLog.boolField(@"fault", bBrakeFault[brakeIdx])
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"fault", @sNa)
    if bBrakeReady[brakeIdx]
        benchLog.boolField(@"stopped", bBrakeStopped[brakeIdx])
    else
        benchLog.textField(@"stopped", @sNa)
    lineEmit()

PRI motorToken(side) : pTok
' Motor token for a side.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* value
' @returns pTok - LEFT, RIGHT or NONE

    case side
        SIDE_LEFT:
            pTok := @sMotLeft
        SIDE_RIGHT:
            pTok := @sMotRight
        other:
            pTok := @sMotNone

PRI boardToken(eBoardRev) : pTok
' Board revision token.
'
' @param eBoardRev - REV_* value
' @returns pTok - REV_A, REV_B or UNKNOWN

    case eBoardRev
        wheelL.REV_A:
            pTok := @sBoardRevA
        wheelL.REV_B:
            pTok := @sBoardRevB
        other:
            pTok := @sBoardUnknown

PRI resultToken(resCode) : pTok
' Hold result token.
'
' @param resCode - RES_* value
' @returns pTok - result token

    case resCode
        RES_OK:
            pTok := @sResOk
        RES_NO_COG:
            pTok := @sResNoCog
        RES_READY_TIMEOUT:
            pTok := @sResReadyTo
        RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT:
            pTok := @sResSteadyTo
        RES_FAULT:
            pTok := @sResFault
        RES_STOP_TIMEOUT:
            pTok := @sResStopTo
        other:
            pTok := @sResNotRun

PRI lineEmit()
' Emit the assembled record as exactly one debug line. One debug() statement carries at most
' 255 bytes of debug data; the whole record travels as a single zero-terminated string
' instead so wider records are never silently truncated by that limit. Brackets every cog-0
' BC- record with CP_EMIT, once, here. Cog 0 only: the watchdog uses wdLineEmit(). The record is
' assembled in benchLog (isp_bench_log, PL-53).

    beat(CP_EMIT)
    debug(zstr_(benchLog.pLine()))
    beat(CP_EMIT)

PRI beat(checkpointId)
' Advance cog 0's heartbeat and record where it is (task 3521 phase B). Called on every pass of
' every wait and measurement loop, and immediately before AND after every library call and every
' lineEmit(), so a watchdog-declared stall's last checkpoint pins it to one statement group.
' COG 0 ONLY: the watchdog cog must never call this, nor anything that calls it (the wheelXxx()
' wrappers, commandMotor(), shutdownMotors(), lineEmit()), or it would feed the very heartbeat it
' is watching.
' PARK: once wdDeclaring is TRUE, beat() never returns. A cog 0 that was slow rather than dead
' (blocked past WD_STALL_MS, then resuming) would otherwise carry on after the watchdog stopped
' the wheels and ended the session, and its next hold could restart a wheel unwatched. Every
' motor command path passes through beat(), so a parked cog 0 cannot reach one.
' Cost inside the 5 ms timed loops: one method call, one hub-long write and one hub-long
' read-add-write -- no wait and no debug(). Each pass is waitms(SAMPLE_MS) followed by the pass
' body, and the window, settle and AT_SPEED loops bound their span by getms(), not by a count,
' so beats cannot shift when a sample is taken within the pass or change any sample's value.
' They lengthen a pass only by their own interpreter time: up to 7 beats in a sampleWindow()
' pass, 5 in a measureZero() pass -- expected to be a small fraction of a millisecond
' (UNVERIFIED: interpreter call timing is not visible in this repo). The visible effect, if
' any, is a slightly lower BC-SENSE samples count over the same WINDOW_MS, and a slightly longer
' span for measureZero()'s fixed ZERO_SAMPLES count.
'
' @param checkpointId - CP_* naming the statement group cog 0 is now inside

    if wdDeclaring
        ' The watchdog has declared a stall, stopped both wheels and ended the session. If cog 0
        '  was only slow rather than dead, it must never command a motor again: park here forever.
        '  A repeat of WD_IDLE_MS, never one long waitms(): see WAITMS_MAX_MS.
        repeat
            waitms(WD_IDLE_MS)
    wdCheckpoint := checkpointId
    wdHeartbeat += 1

PRI checkpointToken(checkpointId) : pTok
' Checkpoint token for BC-WATCHDOG. Safe from either cog: it only returns a DAT address.
'
' @param checkpointId - CP_* naming the statement group cog 0 is now inside
' @returns pTok - checkpoint token; UNKNOWN for a value that is not a CP_* id

    case checkpointId
        CP_MAIN_INIT:
            pTok := @sCpMainInit
        CP_MAIN_BANNER:
            pTok := @sCpMainBanner
        CP_MAIN_PLAN:
            pTok := @sCpMainPlan
        CP_MAIN_RUN:
            pTok := @sCpMainRun
        CP_MAIN_SHUTDOWN:
            pTok := @sCpMainShutdown
        CP_MAIN_END:
            pTok := @sCpMainEnd
        CP_PREFLIGHT_LEFT:
            pTok := @sCpPreLeft
        CP_PREFLIGHT_RIGHT:
            pTok := @sCpPreRight
        CP_HOLD:
            pTok := @sCpHold
        CP_START_SIDE:
            pTok := @sCpStartSide
        CP_LIB_START:
            pTok := @sCpLibStart
        CP_LOOP_WAITREADY:
            pTok := @sCpWaitReady
        CP_LIB_STARTSENSE:
            pTok := @sCpLibSense
        CP_LOOP_ZERO:
            pTok := @sCpZero
        CP_LIB_COMMAND:
            pTok := @sCpLibCommand
        CP_LOOP_ATSPEED:
            pTok := @sCpAtSpeed
        CP_LOOP_STEADY:
            pTok := @sCpSteady
        CP_LOOP_SETTLE:
            pTok := @sCpSettle
        CP_LOOP_WINDOW:
            pTok := @sCpWindow
        CP_LOOP_WAITSTOP:
            pTok := @sCpWaitStop
        CP_LIB_STOP_LEFT:
            pTok := @sCpStopLeft
        CP_LIB_STOP_RIGHT:
            pTok := @sCpStopRight
        CP_LIB_INTEGRITY:
            pTok := @sCpLibInteg
        CP_LIB_DRVSTATE:
            pTok := @sCpLibDrvState
        CP_LIB_COGUP:
            pTok := @sCpLibCogUp
        CP_LIB_ISREADY:
            pTok := @sCpLibIsReady
        CP_LIB_ISSTOPPED:
            pTok := @sCpLibIsStopped
        CP_LIB_TELEMETRY:
            pTok := @sCpLibTelemetry
        CP_LIB_CURRENT:
            pTok := @sCpLibCurrent
        CP_LIB_TICKS:
            pTok := @sCpLibTicks
        CP_LIB_OFFSETS:
            pTok := @sCpLibOffsets
        CP_LIB_RPM:
            pTok := @sCpLibRpm
        CP_LIB_BOARDTYPE:
            pTok := @sCpLibBoardType
        CP_LIB_CONSTANTS:
            pTok := @sCpLibConstants
        CP_EMIT:
            pTok := @sCpEmit
        CP_NOTE:
            pTok := @sCpNote
        CP_STEER:
            pTok := @sCpSteer
        CP_SPACER_LOOP:
            pTok := @sCpSpacerLoop
        CP_LIB_STEER_START:
            pTok := @sCpSteerStart
        CP_LOOP_STEER_RDY:
            pTok := @sCpSteerReady
        CP_STEER_DRIVE:
            pTok := @sCpSteerDrive
        CP_LIB_STEER_STOP:
            pTok := @sCpSteerStop
        CP_LOOP_STEER_STOP:
            pTok := @sCpSteerStopWt
        CP_LIB_STEER_READ:
            pTok := @sCpSteerRead
        CP_BRAKE:
            pTok := @sCpBrake
        CP_LIB_BRAKE_START:
            pTok := @sCpBrakeStart
        CP_LIB_HOLDATSTOP:
            pTok := @sCpHoldAtStop
        CP_BRAKE_SETTLE:
            pTok := @sCpBrakeSettle
        CP_BRAKE_DRIVE:
            pTok := @sCpBrakeDrive
        CP_LIB_STEER_ERROR:
            pTok := @sCpSteerError
        other:
            pTok := @sCpUnknown

PRI watchdog() | lastSeenBeat, lastChangeMs, msSinceBeat
' Watch cog 0's heartbeat from a second cog (task 3521 phase B). Samples every WD_POLL_MS and
' declares a stall once wdHeartbeat has not advanced for WD_STALL_MS (desk trace at WD_STALL_MS).
' Runs forever; declareStall() never returns. Touches no motor unless it declares a stall.
'
' @local lastSeenBeat - wdHeartbeat at the previous sample
' @local lastChangeMs - getms() at the sample that saw wdHeartbeat change
' @local msSinceBeat - ms since that sample

    lastSeenBeat := wdHeartbeat
    lastChangeMs := getms()
    repeat
        waitms(WD_POLL_MS)
        if wdHeartbeat <> lastSeenBeat
            lastSeenBeat := wdHeartbeat
            lastChangeMs := getms()
        else
            msSinceBeat := getms() - lastChangeMs
            if msSinceBeat >= WD_STALL_MS
                declareStall(msSinceBeat)                   ' never returns

PRI declareStall(msSinceBeat)
' Cog 0 has not advanced for at least WD_STALL_MS: record where it was and both wheels' state,
' stop both wheels, report, end the session, then idle forever. Runs in the watchdog cog.
' ORDER: snapshot, then stop, then emit. The snapshot is taken before the stop, so BC-WATCHDOG2
' reports the wheels as the stall left them; the stop comes before this cog's first debug(), so
' no debug() it makes can hold a wheel running (cog 0 may have stalled inside a debug() of its
' own). wdDeclaring is set first, before anything else, so main() -- which tests it immediately
' before it would cogstop this cog -- never stops a declaration in progress. Calls
' wheelL.stop()/wheelR.stop() directly, never shutdownMotors(), which beats. Task 3521 phase D:
' also steering.stop() directly, never steerStop(), which beats, so a stall during the steering
' phase stops its two wheels and its sense cog too (a no-op outside that phase). Spacer cogs a
' stall leaves running are idle and touch no pin; they are not stopped here.
'
' @param msSinceBeat - ms since the sample that last saw wdHeartbeat change

    wdDeclaring := TRUE
    wdSnapshot()
    wdLog.cogEventBegin()
    wheelL.stop()
    wheelR.stop()
    steering.stop()
    emitWatchdog(msSinceBeat)
    emitWatchdog2()
    wdEmitEnd()
    ' QUOTED, not backticked -- matches main()'s own marker exactly.
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
    ' A repeat of WD_IDLE_MS, never one long waitms(): see WAITMS_MAX_MS.
    repeat
        waitms(WD_IDLE_MS)

PRI wdSnapshot() | holdIdx
' Copy, in the watchdog cog, everything BC-WATCHDOG and BC-WATCHDOG2 report into the wdSnap* DAT
' longs: cog 0's checkpoint, hold, side, that hold's result and holdsRun, then each wheel's
' driver telemetry. Every wheel value is read directly through a single-read getter -- never
' through a wheelXxx() wrapper, which would beat.
'
' @local holdIdx - wdHoldIdx, read once

    wdSnapCheckpoint := wdCheckpoint
    holdIdx := wdHoldIdx
    wdSnapHoldIdx := holdIdx
    wdSnapSide := wdSide
    wdSnapResult := RES_NOT_RUN
    if (holdIdx >= HOLD_ZERO) and (holdIdx <= HOLD_COUNT - 1)
        wdSnapResult := holdResultCode[holdIdx]
    wdSnapHoldsRun := holdsRun
    wdSnapDuty[WD_SLOT_LEFT], wdSnapErr[WD_SLOT_LEFT], wdSnapSenseI[WD_SLOT_LEFT], _, _, _, _, _ := wheelL.testGetTelemetry()
    wdSnapMotorCog[WD_SLOT_LEFT] := wheelL.testGetMotorCog()
    wdSnapDrvState[WD_SLOT_LEFT] := wheelL.getDriverState()
    wdSnapFault[WD_SLOT_LEFT] := wheelL.isFaultSignal()
    wdSnapTicks[WD_SLOT_LEFT] := wheelL.getRawHallTicks()
    wdSnapDuty[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], wdSnapErr[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], wdSnapSenseI[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], _, _, _, _, _ := wheelR.testGetTelemetry()
    wdSnapMotorCog[WD_SLOT_RIGHT] := wheelR.testGetMotorCog()
    wdSnapDrvState[WD_SLOT_RIGHT] := wheelR.getDriverState()
    wdSnapFault[WD_SLOT_RIGHT] := wheelR.isFaultSignal()
    wdSnapTicks[WD_SLOT_RIGHT] := wheelR.getRawHallTicks()

PRI emitWatchdog(msSinceBeat) | bHoldValid
' Emit BC-WATCHDOG from the watchdog cog: cog 0's last checkpoint, how long it has been silent,
' the hold and wheel it was on, that hold's result, holds run, and whether the watchdog stack's
' sentinel is intact. hold and result print NA outside a hold (banner, preflight, end).
' Worst case: tag(11) + checkpoint(16) + checkpoint_tok(26) + since_ms(20) + hold(10) +
' motor(12) + result(22) + holds_run(15) + stack_ok(15) = 147 bytes.
'
' @param msSinceBeat - ms since the sample that last saw wdHeartbeat change
'
' @local bHoldValid - TRUE when the snapshot hold index names a hold

    bHoldValid := (wdSnapHoldIdx >= HOLD_ZERO) and (wdSnapHoldIdx <= HOLD_COUNT - 1)
    wdLog.begin(@"BC-WATCHDOG")
    wdLog.numField(@"checkpoint", wdSnapCheckpoint, LIM_TINY)
    wdLog.tokenField(@"checkpoint_tok", checkpointToken(wdSnapCheckpoint), TOKMAX_CP)
    wdLog.numField(@"since_ms", msSinceBeat, LIM_MID)
    if bHoldValid
        wdLog.numField(@"hold", wdSnapHoldIdx, LIM_TINY)
    else
        wdLog.textField(@"hold", @sNa)
    wdLog.tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(wdSnapSide), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    if bHoldValid
        wdLog.tokenField(@"result", resultToken(wdSnapResult), TOKMAX_RESULT)
    else
        wdLog.textField(@"result", @sNa)
    wdLog.numField(@"holds_run", wdSnapHoldsRun, LIM_TINY)
    wdLog.boolField(@"stack_ok", (wdStackSentinel == WD_STACK_SENTINEL))
    wdLineEmit()

PRI emitWatchdog2()
' Emit BC-WATCHDOG2 from the watchdog cog: both wheels' driver state as the snapshot caught it,
' before the watchdog stopped them. cog is testGetMotorCog()'s raw value (cog id + 1, 0 when not
' running); state is getDriverState(); fault is isFaultSignal().
' Worst case: tag(12) + per wheel [cog(11) + state(13) + fault(14) + duty(18) + err(17) +
' sense_mV(19) + ticks(21) = 113] x 2 = 238 bytes.

    wdLog.begin(@"BC-WATCHDOG2")
    wdLog.numField(@"l_cog", wdSnapMotorCog[WD_SLOT_LEFT], LIM_TINY)
    wdLog.numField(@"l_state", wdSnapDrvState[WD_SLOT_LEFT], LIM_TINY)
    wdLog.boolField(@"l_fault", wdSnapFault[WD_SLOT_LEFT])
    wdLog.numField(@"l_duty", wdSnapDuty[WD_SLOT_LEFT], LIM_MID)
    wdLog.numField(@"l_err", wdSnapErr[WD_SLOT_LEFT], LIM_MID)
    wdLog.numField(@"l_sense_mV", wdSnapSenseI[WD_SLOT_LEFT], LIM_SMALL)
    wdLog.numField(@"l_ticks", wdSnapTicks[WD_SLOT_LEFT], LIM_BIG)
    wdLog.numField(@"r_cog", wdSnapMotorCog[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], LIM_TINY)
    wdLog.numField(@"r_state", wdSnapDrvState[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], LIM_TINY)
    wdLog.boolField(@"r_fault", wdSnapFault[WD_SLOT_RIGHT])
    wdLog.numField(@"r_duty", wdSnapDuty[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], LIM_MID)
    wdLog.numField(@"r_err", wdSnapErr[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], LIM_MID)
    wdLog.numField(@"r_sense_mV", wdSnapSenseI[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], LIM_SMALL)
    wdLog.numField(@"r_ticks", wdSnapTicks[WD_SLOT_RIGHT], LIM_BIG)
    wdLineEmit()

PRI wdEmitEnd()
' Emit BC-END from the watchdog cog with exit WATCHDOG. Same fields in the same order as
' emitEnd(); lib_abort is FALSE and trap is NA because no abort trap delivered this end.
' Worst case: tag(6) + exit(14) + preflight_ok(19) + holds_run(15) + lib_abort(16) + trap(16) =
' 86 bytes.

    wdLog.begin(@"BC-END")
    wdLog.tokenField(@"exit", @sExitWatchdog, TOKMAX_EXIT)
    wdLog.boolField(@"preflight_ok", bPreflightOk)
    wdLog.numField(@"holds_run", holdsRun, LIM_TINY)
    wdLog.boolField(@"lib_abort", FALSE)
    wdLog.textField(@"trap", @sNa)
    wdLineEmit()

PRI wdLineEmit()
' Emit the assembled watchdog record as one debug line. Mirrors lineEmit() against the watchdog's own
' builder, wdLog (cog 0 may be stalled mid-record in benchLog), without the beats.

    debug(zstr_(wdLog.pLine()))

